window.GOHUD_SEARCH["en"]={"p":["index.html","install.html","ai.html","widgets.html","widgets-catalog.html","widgets-popups.html","widgets-surfaces.html","widgets-messages.html","widgets-hud.html","widgets-feedback.html","widgets-forms.html","widgets-shapes.html","widgets-overlays.html","widgets-style.html","theming.html","theming-presets.html","theming-tokens.html","theming-opacity.html","theming-skins.html","theming-own.html","theming-contrast.html","icons.html"],"n":["Overview","Install","Go HUD Skill","Widgets","Widgets-Catalog","Widgets-Popups","Widgets-Surfaces","Widgets-Messages","Widgets-Hud","Widgets-Feedback","Widgets-Forms","Widgets-Shapes","Widgets-Overlays","Widgets-Style","Theming","Theming-Presets","Theming-Tokens","Theming-Opacity","Theming-Skins","Theming-Own","Theming-Contrast","Icons"],"d":[[0,"new","New: arcade, comic, Material 3 and a look for kids",0,"Four new families join default, sci-fi and medieval — fourteen built-in looks now, each in dark and light. Every widget, popup and HUD piece takes them with no change to your code: switch the preset and the whole screen follows. material_light material_dark kids_light kids_dark comic_light comic_dark arcade_light arcade_dark Material 3 — for app screens Material 3 Expressive, measured against the official M3 tokens: pill buttons with a 40dp plate inside the 48dp touch target, 28dp dialogs and sheets, filled cards, outlined fields and the Expressive slider. The app components — navigation bar, app bar, FAB, search bar, chips, progress and the date picker — follow the M3 component tokens, and titles are set in the bundled Roboto. For shops, settings, inboxes and every screen that should feel like an app. Kids — the toy box Made for children: every key, row and panel is a jelly candy with a chunky outline and a solid lip that sinks when pressed, each kind of control in its own crayon colour. Quick slots are candy blocks, badges are stickers, the joystick is a rainbow, windows get a sunny title ribbon and a round candy close button, and a press squishes. Sizes and your project's font stay exactly as they were. Comic — bold ink Every face is a comic-book panel: the surface colour inside a bold ink outline, with a hard shadow behind it that goes when the face is pressed. One setting turns every shadow on or off, two more set the outline width and the shadow size, and one call does the same for a single widget. Windows get a yellow title caption. Arcade — painted keys Every key is painted — a gradient, a white gloss and a lip that sinks when pressed, in a navy ink outline — and labelled in white with an ink outline: green to play, blue for the rest, red to delete. Boards are thick, a coloured frame round a pale well, and windows get a gold title banner and a round red close key. Material 3 in detail → · Kids in detail → · Arcade, widget by widget ↓ · Comic, widget by widget ↓ · The same popup in all fourteen looks →","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MATERIAL_LIGHT) # or MATERIAL_DARK GoUi.use_preset(&\"kids_light\") # or &\"kids_dark\" GoUi.use_preset(&\"comic_light\") # or &\"comic_dark\" GoUi.use_preset(&\"arcade_light\") # or &\"arcade_dark\"",-1],[0,"arcade","Arcade: painted keys and thick boards",0,"The newest look dresses every screen like an arcade cabinet. Every key is painted — a gradient from a light top to a deeper bottom, a white gloss stroke and a lip that sinks when pressed, all inside a navy ink outline — and its label is white with an ink outline. Every board is thick: a coloured frame with its own gloss round a pale well. arcade_light puts white boards on a sky-blue page; arcade_dark puts navy boards on a night page. Every picture below is a real gohud screen — the same code, one preset line. arcade_light · the gallery arcade_dark · the gallery GoDialogs GoSheet GoCoachMark GoDrawer GoPopover GoDialogs.alert() GoSnackbar","GoUi.use_preset(&\"arcade_light\") # or &\"arcade_dark\"",-1],[0,"every-key-painted","Every key painted",1,"GoStyle.button() GoStyle.tabs() Segmented keys Toggles and check boxes GoStyle.card() GoForm GoStyle.choice_grid() GoSlotGrid List rows GoDatePicker GoStyle.slider() GoStyle.radio_group() GoStyle.filter_chip() GoSearchBar GoStepper GoTable GoNavBar GoTimePicker GoCodeInput GoWheelPicker","",1],[0,"at-night-arcade-dark","At night: arcade_dark",1,"On a dark page the ink becomes the page itself, much deeper, and the paints stay just as bright. GoStyle.button() at night GoBar GoStyle.hud_panel() GoSlot GoJoystick Alerts GoFab GoRewardCalendar Segmented keys GoTabView GoScroll Toggles and check boxes GoStyle.chip() GoSlotGrid GoRangeSlider GoPagination GoBadge","",1],[0,"how-the-arcade-look-works","How the arcade look works",1,"The face Every key and board is a GoStyleBoxArcade: an ink outline, a gradient body, a lip and a gloss, drawn inside the control's own rectangle — a key keeps its size from state to state, and a press only sinks it. Labels that read A white label with an ink outline reads on any paint the outline stands off — WCAG counts the outline as part of the letter. Every paint is moved until its label clears 4.6:1 at every height of the gradient. Windows A window's title sits on a gold banner in white letters outlined in ink, next to a round red close key. Dialogs, sheets, drawers and popovers are thick framed boards. One key can take its own colour — an orange shop key in a pause menu: Arcade in detail → · The same popup in all fourteen looks →","menu.add_child(GoStyle.arcade_paint(GoStyle.button(\"Shop\", _shop), Color(\"#FF8A1E\")))",1],[0,"comic","Comic: bold ink and a hard shadow",0,"The comic look draws every face like a panel in a comic book — the surface colour inside a bold ink outline, with a hard, solid shadow dropped down and to the right. comic_light inks black on a paper-cream page with a cobalt primary; comic_dark inks cream on a night page with a yellow primary. Every picture below is a real gohud screen — the same code, one preset line. comic_light · the gallery comic_dark · the gallery GoSheet GoCoachMark GoDrawer GoPopover","GoUi.use_preset(&\"comic_light\") # or &\"comic_dark\"",-1],[0,"every-widget-inked","Every widget, inked",1,"Buttons, toggles, tabs, sliders, cards, forms, tables, pickers and chips all wear the ink — you do not style them one by one. Press a key and its shadow goes: the face sinks into its place, like a stamp. Disabled faces lose their shadow and fade, so what can be pressed stands out from what cannot. GoStyle.button() — every kind Toggles and check boxes Radio buttons GoStyle.tabs() Segmented pills GoStyle.slider() Selects GoStyle.card() GoForm List rows GoTable GoDatePicker GoTimePicker GoStepper Filter chips GoNavBar GoInputGroup GoSplitButton GoPagination","",5],[0,"at-night-comic-dark","At night: comic_dark",1,"On a dark page a black outline would vanish, so comic_dark draws it in cream and drops a faint shadow tinted with the same ink. The HUD pieces — quick slots, bars, the joystick and the reward calendar — follow the same rules. GoStyle.button() at night GoSlot GoBar GoJoystick Alerts GoSlotGrid GoRewardCalendar Chips GoRangeSlider GoSearchBar GoFab","",5],[0,"how-the-comic-look-works","How the comic look works",1,"One StyleBox for every face Every face is a GoStyleBoxComic: a fill, an outline and a shadow, drawn inside the control’s own rectangle. It reads the outline and shadow sizes from GoConfig each time it draws, so one setting changes the whole screen at once. Pressed means flat A pressed key drops its shadow and moves into its place. Hover keeps the shadow; focus adds an inner ink ring that never covers the outline; disabled faces lose the shadow and fade. The skin inks the rest GoSkinComic inks what code draws: quick slots, chips, badges, avatars, notices, the navigation bar, the FAB, the date cells and the joystick, whose knob casts a shadow. Windows get a caption A window’s title sits on a yellow caption, like the narration box of a comic, next to an inked round close button. Dialogs, sheets, drawers and popovers are opaque inked panels. Readable day and night Both palettes pass the same WCAG contrast checks as every other preset, including pressed and disabled keys. When a caption colour would sit too close to the page, its outline falls back to the page colour. No layout changes The outline and shadow fit inside each control and the padding stays as the theme gave it, so a screen laid out in another look keeps its layout — and your project’s font.","",5],[0,"three-settings-and-one-call","Three settings and one call",1,"Three GoConfig settings change every comic face at once. Nothing is rebuilt — the screen redraws as you set them. One widget can go its own way, whatever the settings say. Pass true as the last argument to include everything inside it. Make a comic of your own. tools/new_theme.py inked --from comic_light copies the palette; change the paper, ink and primary colours and run tools/make_theme.py inked. The ink, the shadow and the skin come along. Comic in detail → · The same popup in all fourteen looks →","GoUi.config.comic_border_width = 2.0 # the outline (dp) — 3 by default GoUi.config.comic_shadow_size = 6.0 # the shadow (dp) — 4 by default GoUi.config.comic_shadow = false # no shadows anywhere GoStyle.comic_shadow(skip_button, false) # this button sits flat GoStyle.comic_shadow(card, true, true) # this card and everything in it keep their shadow GoStyle.comic_border(title, 5.0) # a thicker outline on this one",5],[0,"showcase","What it looks like in a game",0,"The medieval and sci-fi presets — character sheets, inventories and quests; forms, grids and prompt cards; angular panels and touch controls. Switching presets is one line of code. Medieval — character, inventory and quests Medieval — forms, grids and prompt cards Sci-fi — angular panels and touch controls All fourteen presets and how to switch them →","",-1],[0,"what","What it takes off your hands",0,"What costs the most time in game UI is not the shape of a button — it is everything that drifts apart between devices. gohud handles that drift in one place. Every measurement is a token Spacing, corners and text sizes are called by name, not written as numbers. Swap the theme and the whole screen moves with it. Visible size ≠ pressable size A close button looks 36dp but its touch target is 48dp. Where crowded slots overlap, the one whose centre is nearer takes the press. Notches and keyboards HUD pieces sit inside the safe area, and an input rises above the virtual keyboard when it appears. Back closes one thing Escape and Android Back close only the topmost surface. Stacked windows do not vanish together. Notices never steal input Press through a snackbar and the button underneath receives it. Focus is not taken either. Icons are asked for by name Widgets only know GoIconSet.CLOSE. Swap the set and every drawing changes without touching a line of code. Icons → Fourteen looks, one line GoUi.use_preset() swaps theme, skin and icons together — rounded, chamfered sci-fi, forged medieval frames, Material 3 app components, kids' jelly candies, comic ink or arcade paint. Legible by measurement Every theme is checked against WCAG, including button states and translucent HUD panels over pure white and pure black. Everything works without enabling the plugin. Enabling it adds a GoRuntime autoload that tracks window size, dp scale and keyboard height, plus project settings for the config resource and the preset — conveniences, not requirements.","",-1],[0,"install","Install gohud",0,"Two ways in. Let your AI agent do it, or drop the folder into your project — there is nothing else to set up. Install","",-1],[0,"start","Quick start",0,"Five lines put a themed screen on the display. See the whole walk-through on the install page. Quick start","",-1],[0,"presets","Change the look — colours and shape",0,"A Theme can only restyle what the engine draws. Rounded corners are the only corners StyleBoxFlat has, and the joystick, quick slots and coach mark are drawn by code — so a theme alone can never change their shape. gohud therefore ships presets: a theme, a skin and an icon set picked as one unit. Preset Look default_dark The original gohud — rounded corners, soft blue accent default_light The same shapes on a light palette scifi_dark Chamfered corners, cyan neon edges and glow, hexagonal joystick, targeting brackets scifi_light The same angular shapes in a bright blueprint palette medieval_dark Dark iron and leather, antique-gold frames, rivets, engraved icons, Cinzel headings medieval_light Parchment, ink and bronze with the same forged frames material_light New Material 3 for app screens — pill buttons, 28dp dialogs, filled cards, an app's navigation bar, FAB and search bar, Roboto material_dark New The same Material 3 shapes on the dark baseline kids_light New The toy box for children — jelly-candy keys with a chunky outline and a lip that sinks when pressed, crayon colours, a sunny page kids_dark New The same toy box on a night-blue page comic_light New Comic-book panels — a bold ink outline and a hard shadow on every face, white panels on a paper-cream page; the shadow, its size and the outline width are settings comic_dark New The same ink on a night page — cream outlines and a yellow primary arcade_light New An arcade cabinet — every key painted with a gradient, a gloss and a lip, labelled in white with an ink outline; thick framed boards on a sky-blue page, a gold title banner on windows arcade_dark New The same bright keys on navy boards and a night page default_dark — rounded corners, soft blue accent default_light — same shapes, light palette scifi_dark — chamfered corners, cyan neon scifi_light — same angular shapes, blueprint palette Those four are the same gallery screen. Not a line of code differs — only the preset name. Button corners, toggle shapes, list rows and input borders all move together.","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MEDIEVAL_DARK) # theme, skin and icons together",-1],[0,"medieval-collection","Medieval collection",1,"medieval_dark pairs iron and leather with antique gold; medieval_light uses parchment and ink. Menu frames carry a rivet and a small corner ornament while the always-visible HUD stays quiet; 16 engraved icons redraw the item names, and only titles and subtitles use the bundled Cinzel font. medieval_dark — iron and leather medieval_light — parchment and ink Both shots are examples/medieval/medieval.tscn, built from the standard widgets. The medieval guide and how to make your own kingdom →","",14],[0,"the-same-screen-on-a-phone-and-on-a-desktop","The same screen on a phone and on a desktop",1,"The gallery shots are a phone in portrait. Below is the same code at 1280×800 — the content stops at a readable width (480dp) and centres, while the HUD stays in the corners. The form steps around floating HUD pieces, but does not move when it is already clear of them: pushing anyway would throw the content off-centre on a wide screen. default_dark · 1280×800 scifi_dark · 1280×800","",14],[0,"the-same-sheet-a-different-look","The same sheet, a different look",1,"Default — rounded card, sticky search row and footer Sci-fi — top accent edge, cut corners, glow Pick one from Project Settings → gohud → Theme → Preset, or set GoConfig.preset. Filling in theme, skin or icons explicitly wins over the preset, so you can take a preset and override just one of them. A new theme is one JSON file. new_theme.py kingdom --from medieval_dark writes a palette that spells out every inherited value; make_theme.py kingdom builds the theme, its control artwork and its skin dials, and the preset appears in the picker. Every setting and dial →","",14],[0,"skin","Skins — where a Theme cannot reach",0,"A skin owns the joystick, quick-slot faces, the coach-mark ring, chips, skeletons, alerts, dividers and section headings. Subclass it and override only what you want changed. Class Shapes it can make GoStyleBoxCut Diagonally cut corners (chamfer), one thickened accent edge, an outer glow GoStyleBoxBracket Corner marks only, without enclosing the content GoStyleBoxMedieval A forged frame with rivets, corner engraving, a bevel highlight and material grain GoStyleBoxJelly A jelly candy — a chunky outline, a solid lip that sinks when pressed, a body lighter on top and a white shine GoStyleBoxComic A comic-book panel — a bold ink outline and a hard drop shadow, both sized by GoConfig while the game runs GoStyleBoxArcade An arcade key or board — a gradient body, a white gloss, a lip that sinks when pressed and an ink outline; a board adds a thick coloured frame round a pale well All six serialise into a Theme resource — which is what lets a theme change shape, not just colour. GoSkinSciFi, GoSkinMedieval, GoSkinMaterial, GoSkinKids, GoSkinComic and GoSkinArcade are the shipped subclasses. What a skin draws — default, kids, Material, medieval, sci-fi …and the comic skin …and the arcade skin GoStyle.box() always returns a StyleBoxFlat, because calling code receives it and adjusts bg_color or corner_radius. Use GoStyle.surface() when a custom shape has to survive.","class_name MySkin extends GoSkin func slot_box(accent: Color, lit: bool) -> StyleBox: var box := GoStyleBoxCut.new() box.bg_color = accent box.cut = 6.0 box.edge_color = accent return box",-1],[0,"widgets","Widgets",0,"The pieces, in one table. Each one in detail → · Every widget with a picture → · Popups and dialogs, the full guide → Class Base What it does GoSurface Control Floating card shell — centre, bottom or anchored placement, sticky header and footer, scrolling body, drag-to-resize GoSheet CanvasLayer Pages rising from the bottom, on their own layer so they sit above the HUD GoDialogs Node Confirmations and alerts you await; destructive for irreversible actions GoForm MarginContainer Width-capped forms that avoid the virtual keyboard and, with avoid_hud, the HUD GoScroll ScrollContainer Touch scrolling; the scrollbar tucks into the card padding GoNotice PanelContainer A snackbar that takes neither input nor focus GoPromptCard PanelContainer A question that does not block the game GoCoachMark Control A guided tour that points at real controls; pressing the target advances GoHudAnchor Control Pins HUD pieces to one of nine safe-area spots GoBar Control Health, mana and experience bars with eased changes GoSlot Button A quick slot — icon, quantity, cooldown and shortcut on one face GoJoystick Control Virtual stick in fixed, follow or relative mode GoIconButton Button Looks small, presses large GoStyle static Buttons, list rows, inputs, chips, tables, tabs and more, made one consistent way","",-1],[0,"waiting-telling-counting","Waiting, telling, counting",1,"Class Base What it does GoSnackbar Node the message that places itself GoSpinner Control a wait with no end in sight GoBadge PanelContainer the unread dot, the NEW tag, the 99+","",19],[0,"forms-and-lists","Forms and lists",1,"Class Base What it does GoField VBoxContainer the row that can be wrong GoInputGroup HBoxContainer an input welded to its button GoCombobox Button a picker that searches GoCodeInput VBoxContainer coupon and gift codes GoTable VBoxContainer sortable headers, selectable rows GoPagination HBoxContainer pages, or a More row","",19],[0,"shapes-games-actually-use","Shapes games actually use",1,"Class Base What it does GoRewardCalendar VBoxContainer daily attendance GoRadar · GoDonut Control stats at a glance GoCarousel VBoxContainer banners and character select GoKbd HBoxContainer key hints that do not lie","",19],[0,"over-the-screen","Over the screen",1,"Class Base What it does GoDrawer CanvasLayer the side panel GoPopover RefCounted the anchored card GoContextMenu RefCounted long-press and right-click GoConsole CanvasLayer the developer console","",19],[0,"ai","Go HUD Skill",0,"gohud ships an AI skill: the whole API, runnable templates and a preview launcher. Paste one block into your coding agent and it installs gohud and knows how to use it. Go HUD Skill","",-1],[0,"readable","Readability is measured, not eyeballed",0,"\"Pretty\" is taste; \"legible\" can be measured. Faint grey text looks fine on a good monitor and disappears on a phone in daylight — picking by eye guarantees it eventually. Every colour pair and every button state's label over the panel it sits on is measured against WCAG, in all fourteen themes. Translucent colours are composited over their real backdrop first — measuring them directly reports a better ratio than the screen shows. Text colours are therefore derived, not chosen: the builder takes the palette entry as a starting point and pushes its lightness until it clears the threshold on every surface it can land on. Change the palette and the contrast follows. The rules and the traps behind them → Checks, releases and this site One entry point runs every check; each part sees something the others cannot. Check What it catches run_tests.sh at four screen sizes Widget behaviour and layout, RTL positions, keyboard focus, runtime skin contrast, every preset new_project_check.sh Hidden dependencies on a host project; with --zip the release as shipped, with --export a Web build check_contrast.py WCAG contrast of every theme file, button states and translucent panels included check_generated.py · check_scaffold.sh Generated themes match their palettes; a throwaway theme builds and passes contrast check_package.py The version taken from package.json, changelog moves and ZIP contents, in temporary copies check_site.py This site's links, anchors, page language, glossary and dial tables Latest recorded run — 2026-09-13, Godot 4.7.2, macOS, Compatibility renderer. 438 of 438 checks at 390×844, 844×390, 768×1024 and 1280×800 in an empty project; 438 of 438 again with the GoRuntime autoload; a Web export; zero contrast failures across the six themes. Physical Android or iOS devices were not part of this run.","python3 addons/gohud/tools/check_contrast.py bash addons/gohud/tools/check_all.sh",-1],[0,"release-versions","Release versions",1,"The version is the one written in package.json — packaging never raises it. To release a new version, change that number first. A successful run sets plugin.cfg and GoUi.VERSION to it and, the first time that version is packaged, moves the Unreleased notes of CHANGELOG.md into a dated entry. Packaging the same version again rebuilds its ZIP and replaces the old one. A failed run changes nothing. The ZIP leaves out this website, the tests, the tools and package.json.","cat addons/gohud/package.json # { \"version\": \"1.1.0\" } bash addons/gohud/tools/release.sh # every check → ZIP → that ZIP in an empty project bash addons/gohud/tools/package.sh # 1.1.0 → builds/1.1.0/gohud-1.1.0.zip",25],[0,"this-site","This site",1,"The pages are plain HTML in www/ — English at the root, Korean in ko/. A GitHub Actions workflow publishes that folder as the site root.","python3 addons/gohud/tools/make_site.py # glossary and skin-dial tables, generated from source python3 addons/gohud/tools/check_site.py # links, anchors, language, glossary, generated tables bash addons/gohud/tools/site_shots.sh /tmp/shots # desktop and phone screenshots of every page",25],[1,"ai-first","Fastest way — let your AI agent install it",0,"One block of text, pasted into Claude Code, Codex, Cursor or Gemini CLI, installs both the skill and the add-on and then explains gohud to you. Nothing below this card is needed if you take that road. Open the Go HUD Skill page →","",-1],[1,"install","Install",0,"Put the add-on folder into your project. There is nothing else to set up.","",-1],[1,"from-the-asset-store-or-a-release-zip","From the Asset Store or a release ZIP",1,"Extract into your project root so you get res://addons/gohud/. That is all. Optionally enable Project → Project Settings → Plugins → gohud.","",29],[1,"as-a-git-submodule","As a git submodule",1,"The repository root is the add-on folder, so it lands exactly where Godot expects it. Edit in place, commit and push inside addons/gohud, then commit the submodule pointer in your game. Tested on Godot 4.7; Godot 4.7 and newer are officially supported. gohud uses APIs introduced in 4.5 (DPITexture, FoldableContainer, accessibility properties), so on anything older it fails while parsing. 4.7 is the supported floor, recorded in GoUi.MIN_ENGINE.","git submodule add https://github.com/thruthesky/gohud.git addons/gohud git submodule update --init git -C addons/gohud checkout v1.0.0 # optional: pin a tag or commit",29],[1,"start","Quick start",0,"Every widget is .new() and add_child() — no scene files, no autoload.","",-1],[1,"pick-a-look-before-building-ui-optional","Pick a look before building UI (optional)",1,"","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.SCIFI_DARK) # default_dark is used when you skip this",32],[1,"a-confirmation-you-await","A confirmation you await",1,"Pass destructive = true (the last argument) and the confirm button is drawn as a filled danger button.","var dialogs := GoDialogs.new() add_child(dialogs) if await dialogs.confirm(\"Delete save\", \"This cannot be undone.\"): delete_save()",32],[1,"a-bottom-sheet-with-a-sticky-search-field-and-fo","A bottom sheet with a sticky search field and footer",1,"Why sticky rows are separate from the scrolling body. Put confirm and cancel in body and a long list pushes them off screen. footer() is always visible.","var sheet := GoSheet.new() add_child(sheet) sheet.open(\"Inventory\") sheet.toolbar().add_child(GoStyle.line_edit(\"Search…\")) sheet.toolbar().visible = true for item in items: sheet.body.add_child(GoStyle.list_button(GoIconSet.BOX, item.name, _use.bind(item), Color.TRANSPARENT, item.description, false)) sheet.footer().add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Close\", sheet.close, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) sheet.footer().visible = true",32],[1,"a-hud-corner","A HUD corner",1,"","var corner := GoHudAnchor.new() corner.spot = GoHudAnchor.Spot.TOP_LEFT corner.landscape_spot = GoHudAnchor.Spot.TOP_RIGHT add_child(corner) var hp := GoBar.new() hp.label_text = \"HP\" hp.ink = GoUi.color(GoTheme.DANGER_FILL) corner.add_child(hp) hp.set_values(320, 500)",32],[1,"content-that-keeps-clear-of-the-hud","Content that keeps clear of the HUD",1,"Each rectangle is avoided in whichever direction costs the least area — downwards on a portrait phone, sideways in landscape. How the HUD avoids itself →","form.avoid_hud = true # keep clear of every visible GoHudAnchor joystick_anchor.reserve_space = false # …except ones that only appear under a finger notice_anchor.avoid_peers = true # a toast settles below the fixed HUD instead of covering it",32],[1,"examples","Examples you can run",0,"Three ways to see gohud before writing a line — none needs a server or an autoload. Example How to open What it shows Gallery examples/gallery/gallery.tscn · F6 Every widget, a picker for every installed preset, and the full icon set Medieval examples/medieval/medieval.tscn · F6 A character sheet, satchel and quest journal; buttons switch iron and parchment and open item details Demo app cd examples/demo && godot A home screen opening the gallery, the 19-chapter guided tour, the showcase screen and the medieval look, with live widgets and one card per class The demo app needs no setup: if the add-on link or the import cache is missing it says so, repairs the folder and reopens itself. Its home screen opens each example inside the same window — press 1–4 or click a row, and the bar across the top brings you back. In the tour, C toggles Cinema mode, F11 fullscreen, Space pauses (or plays the current widget while exploring), the arrows change chapters and Escape returns to Start. Using an AI coding agent? Open all three with one command →","cd examples/demo && godot # home screen; links and imports on first run bash examples/demo/run.sh # the same app, from the add-on root bash examples/demo/run.sh -- --open=gallery # skip the home screen bash examples/demo/run.sh -- --explore=surfaces # open straight onto one tour chapter bash examples/demo/run.sh --record /tmp/gohud-demo.avi # 1080p / 60 fps recording of the tour",-1],[2,"copy","Copy this into your coding agent",0,"Open your Godot project in the agent, paste the block, send it. It installs the skill and the add-on, then tells you what gohud can do. Open a terminal in your Godot project folder and start your coding agent there — for example claude. Press Copy on the block below, paste it into the agent and send it. When it is done, restart the agent if it asks you to, then ask it: What can gohud do? The block is written in English on purpose — that is what every agent reads most reliably. You can ask your own questions in any language; the skill answers in the language you write in.","Install gohud for this Godot 4.7+ project, then use it for all game UI (menus, HUD bars, quick slots, dialogs, bottom sheets, forms, themes). 1. Install the gohud AI skill. Claude Code - run these two commands in a shell: claude plugin marketplace add thruthesky/gohud claude plugin install gohud@gohud Any other agent (Codex, Cursor, Gemini CLI, ...): git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/thruthesky/gohud.git /tmp/gohud Copy /tmp/gohud/skills/gohud into whichever of these folders this agent reads: ~/.claude/skills/gohud, .claude/skills/gohud, .agents/skills/gohud. 2. Install the add-on itself, unless addons/gohud/plugin.cfg already exists here. In a git repository: git submodule add https://github.com/thruthesky/gohud.git addons/gohud Otherwise copy the clone to addons/gohud without its .git folder. Then run: godot --headless --path . --import (If godot is not on PATH, ask me where Godot 4.7+ is.) 3. Check the result: addons/gohud/plugin.cfg exists and the import printed no \"SCRIPT ERROR\" or \"Parse Error\" lines. 4. A new skill loads when the agent starts. Tell me if I have to restart you, then tell me what gohud can do and how to preview it. Docs: https://thruthesky.github.io/gohud/",-1],[2,"claude-code","Or type two commands — Claude Code",0,"This installs the skill as a Claude Code plugin. In a terminal: Already inside Claude Code? Type these instead: Then restart Claude Code and type /gohud:features — if it lists gohud's features, the skill is in. The add-on itself still goes into addons/gohud: Install →","claude plugin marketplace add thruthesky/gohud claude plugin install gohud@gohud /plugin marketplace add thruthesky/gohud /plugin install gohud@gohud",-1],[2,"agents","Where each agent keeps skills",0,"Installing by hand instead? Put the skills/gohud folder in the place your agent reads. The first one that exists wins. Agent Where the folder goes How commands look Claude Code — plugin claude plugin install gohud@gohud /gohud:preview · /gohud:features Claude Code — skill only ~/.claude/skills/gohud /gohud preview · /gohud features Claude Code — this project only .claude/skills/gohud /gohud preview Codex · Cursor · Gemini CLI — others .agents/skills/gohud —","",-1],[2,"commands","The commands you get",0,"","",-1],[2,"gohud-preview-the-widget-gallery","/gohud:preview — the widget gallery",1,"Opens the gallery: every widget, a picker for every preset and the full icon set. Type it inside your Godot project and it uses your addons/gohud; without one it uses the copy bundled with the plugin, or a fresh clone. It runs in a throwaway sandbox project, so your autoloads and import cache are left alone, and the window stays open until you close it.","",42],[2,"gohud-preview-demo-the-19-chapter-guided-tour","/gohud:preview demo — the 19-chapter guided tour",1,"Opens the demo on its start screen. Start demo plays the tour with real input; Explore widgets lets you try one widget by hand. The keys listed under Examples work here too.","",42],[2,"many-other-commands","Many other commands",1,"Command What it does /gohud:preview medieval The character sheet, satchel and quest journal in the medieval presets /gohud:preview demo --explore hud The demo opened straight onto one chapter — hud buttons inputs selection lists data states surfaces prompt touch coach scrolling forms anchors theming /gohud:preview gallery --preset scifi_dark The gallery in one preset; add --phone for a 390×844 phone window or --size 1920x1080 for any size /gohud:preview res://ui/main_menu.tscn A scene of your own project, run inside that project /gohud:preview list Every target, preset id and demo chapter key /gohud:preview gallery --check A headless smoke test with no window — fails on script errors /gohud:features Every feature, grouped, one line of code each /gohud:features hud One area in depth — surfaces hud style theming icons i18n accessibility config You need Godot 4.7 or newer on your PATH for the preview commands.","",42],[2,"ask","Or just ask",0,"Or just ask. The skill teaches the agent gohud's whole API, so plain requests work too — \"Build a pause menu with gohud\". Installed as a plain skill in ~/.claude/skills/gohud, the commands take a space: /gohud preview demo, /gohud features. Previews need Godot 4.7 or newer on your PATH, or pass --godot /path/to/godot.","",-1],[4,"layout","Layout (15)",0,"GoScaffold An app screen wired together: bar, scrolling page, bottom bar, FAB and drawer. extends Control GoTopBar Items along the top edge in one to three slots; the centre stays centred. extends GoEdgeBar GoBottomBar Items along the bottom edge, clear of the gesture bar. extends GoEdgeBar GoLeftSideBar Up to three tiers down the left edge. extends GoSideBar GoRightSideBar Up to three tiers down the right edge. extends GoSideBar GoSideBar The side bar both of those are; it keeps its side in right-to-left languages. extends GoEdgeBar GoEdgeBar The rules every edge bar shares: slots, spreading, pinning to the edge, the safe area. extends Container GoGrid Columns of exactly equal width — a fixed count, or as many as fit. extends Container GoForm A form that caps its width and keeps clear of the keyboard and the HUD. extends MarginContainer GoScroll Touch scrolling that works from anywhere on the content; right-to-left aware. extends ScrollContainer GoHudAnchor Pins HUD pieces to one of nine safe-area spots. extends Control GoStyle.column · row · wrap_row Columns, rows and wrapping rows with gaps from the theme. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.responsive_grid · aspect A grid that adds columns as it widens; a box that keeps its ratio. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.padding · spacer · divider Padding, a spacer that takes the room left over, a divider line. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.foldable · section A section heading, and a section that folds open. a function of GoStyle","var page := GoStyle.column() var screen := GoScaffold.make(\"Inbox\", page, true) screen.set_fab(GoFab.make(GoIconSet.EDIT)) add_child(screen) var bar := GoTopBar.make(3) bar.add_start(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.BACK, go_back, -1, &\"back\")) bar.add_center(GoStyle.label(\"Stage 3\")) bar.add_end(GoStyle.chip(\"1,250\")) var actions := GoBottomBar.make(1, GoBottomBar.Justify.SPACE_BETWEEN) for name in [\"Attack\", \"Guard\", \"Run\"]: actions.add_start(GoStyle.button(name)) screen.add_child(actions) var tools := GoLeftSideBar.make(3) tools.add_start(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.MENU, open_menu, -1, &\"menu\")) tools.add_end(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.USER, open_profile, -1, &\"profile\")) screen.add_child(tools) var tools := GoRightSideBar.make(3) tools.add_start(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.SETTINGS, open_settings, -1, &\"settings\")) tools.add_center(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.SEARCH, find, -1, &\"search\")) screen.add_child(tools) var rail := GoRightSideBar.make(1, GoSideBar.Justify.CENTER) rail.add_start(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.MAP, open_map, -1, &\"map\")) var bar := GoTopBar.make(1) bar.justify = GoEdgeBar.Justify.SPACE_BETWEEN bar.pin_to_edge = GoEdgeBar.Pin.ALWAYS var cards := GoGrid.make(1, 160.0) for item in items: cards.add_child(GoStyle.item_card(item)) var form := GoForm.new() form.avoid_hud = true form.add_child(GoScroll.new()) add_child(form) var list := GoScroll.new() list.add_child(GoStyle.column()) var strip := GoScroll.horizontal() var corner := GoHudAnchor.new() corner.spot = GoHudAnchor.Spot.TOP_LEFT corner.add_child(GoStyle.hud_panel()) var page := GoStyle.column() var line := GoStyle.row() var chips := GoStyle.wrap_row() var tiles := GoStyle.responsive_grid(160) var thumb := GoStyle.aspect(16.0 / 9.0) var pad := GoStyle.padding(16) line.add_child(GoStyle.spacer()) page.add_child(GoStyle.divider()) page.add_child(GoStyle.section(\"Sound\", false)) var more := GoStyle.foldable(\"Advanced\", true, null, false)",-1],[4,"windows","Windows and overlays (9)",0,"GoSurface A floating window — centred, from the bottom, or anchored to a control. extends Control GoSheet A bottom sheet with pages, back navigation and a sticky footer. extends CanvasLayer GoDialogs Confirm and alert windows you await; alerts wait their turn. extends Node GoDialogs.choose One of a few options — a bottom sheet on a phone, a card on a desktop. a function of GoDialogs GoDrawer A panel that slides in from the left or the right. extends CanvasLayer GoPopover An info card beside what was pressed; one at a time. extends RefCounted GoContextMenu Long press or right click for a menu; a moving finger cancels it. extends RefCounted GoCoachMark A guided tour that points at real controls. extends Control GoConsole A developer console with commands and history; off in release builds. extends CanvasLayer","var window := GoSurface.new() window.set_title(\"Settings\") window.close_requested.connect(window.queue_free) layer.add_child(window) var sheet := GoSheet.new() add_child(sheet) sheet.open(\"Inventory\") sheet.body.add_child(bag_list) var dialogs := GoDialogs.new() add_child(dialogs) if await dialogs.confirm(\"Delete save\", \"This cannot be undone.\", \"\", \"\", \"\", {}, true): delete_save() var index := await dialogs.choose(\"Sort by\", [\"Newest\", \"Price\", \"Rating\"]) if index >= 0: sort_by(index) var drawer := GoDrawer.new() add_child(drawer) drawer.side = GoDrawer.Side.RIGHT drawer.open(\"Bag\") GoPopover.open(slot, GoStyle.item_card(item, false)) GoContextMenu.attach(slot, [{\"text\": \"Use\"}, {\"text\": \"Drop\", \"danger\": true}]) var tour := GoCoachMark.new() add_child(tour) tour.start([{\"target\": bag_button, \"title\": \"Bag\", \"body\": \"Your items live here.\"}]) var console := GoConsole.new() add_child(console) console.register(\"give\", \"Grant an item\", give_item)",-1],[4,"messages","Messages and waiting (12)",0,"GoSnackbar A message at the bottom that queues and can carry buttons. extends Node GoNotice A notice that never takes input or focus. extends PanelContainer GoPromptCard A question that does not stop the game — an invite, a trade. extends PanelContainer GoBanner A message that stays on the page until it is dealt with. extends PanelContainer GoSpinner A wait; turns a button into a spinner in place, so it cannot be pressed twice. extends Control GoBadge The unread dot, the NEW tag and 99+, hung on a corner. extends PanelContainer GoProgress Progress as a line or a ring, wavy or flat; indeterminate while the size is unknown. extends Control GoLoadingIndicator The Material 3 Expressive wait mark that changes shape; still under reduce_motion. extends Control GoRefresh Pull a list down at its top to reload it. extends Control GoStyle.alert An inline message in the info, success, warning or danger tone. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.skeleton · empty_state A placeholder while loading, and a message for an empty list. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.tooltip_node A tooltip in the theme's style that never splits its words. a function of GoStyle","var snack := GoSnackbar.new() add_child(snack) if await snack.post({\"text\": \"Item dropped\", \"actions\": [\"Undo\"]}) == 0: restore_item() var notice := GoNotice.new() hud.add_child(notice) notice.show_text(\"Saved\", GoTheme.SUCCESS) var invite := GoPromptCard.new() invite.set_title(\"Party invite from Ann\") invite.set_actions([{\"text\": \"Accept\", \"action\": accept, \"primary\": true}]) var offline := GoBanner.make(\"You're offline.\", [{\"text\": \"Retry\", \"action\": reconnect}], GoIconSet.WARNING) page.add_child(offline) GoSpinner.busy(buy_button, true) await shop.buy(item) GoSpinner.busy(buy_button, false) GoBadge.attach(mail_button, unread) GoBadge.attach(shop_button, 0, \"NEW\") var upload := GoProgress.linear() upload.value = 0.4 var ring := GoProgress.circular(true) var wait := GoLoadingIndicator.new() wait.contained = true page.add_child(wait) var refresh := GoRefresh.attach(feed) refresh.refresh_requested.connect(func() -> void: await reload_posts() refresh.finish()) page.add_child(GoStyle.alert(\"Maintenance at 3 AM\", GoTheme.WARNING)) page.add_child(GoStyle.skeleton(200)) page.add_child(GoStyle.empty_state(GoIconSet.BOX, \"No items yet\", false)) func _make_custom_tooltip(text: String) -> Object: return GoStyle.tooltip_node(text)",-1],[4,"navigation","App navigation (13)",0,"GoAppBar The top app bar; lifts when the page scrolls; medium and large titles. extends PanelContainer GoNavBar Three to five destinations along the bottom; a rail on wide screens. extends PanelContainer GoNavBar.drawer_list Full-width destination rows for a drawer. a function of GoNavBar GoFab The screen's main action floating in the corner; 40–96dp or extended with a label. extends Button GoSearchBar The rounded search field with a clear button and trailing actions. extends PanelContainer GoSplitButton A main action with its variants behind an arrow. extends HBoxContainer GoTabView Tabs across the row over pages you swipe between. extends VBoxContainer GoStyle.tabs A tab row, at the start or spread over the row; the line runs the full width. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.bottom_app_bar The bottom bar with icon actions and a FAB. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.toolbar A floating pill of icon actions. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.breadcrumb Where you are, as a path you can step back along. a function of GoStyle GoPagination Numbered pages that keep the current one centred, or a single Load more row. extends HBoxContainer GoCarousel Banners and character select that never turn on their own unless asked. extends VBoxContainer","var bar := GoAppBar.make(\"Inbox\", GoIconSet.MENU, open_drawer) bar.add_action(GoIconSet.SEARCH, &\"search\", open_search) bar.follow(list) var nav := GoNavBar.make([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.HOME, \"text\": \"Home\"}, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.BELL, \"text\": \"Alerts\", \"badge\": 3}], 0, show_tab) var rail := GoNavBar.rail([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.HOME, \"text\": \"Home\"}]) drawer.body.add_child(GoNavBar.drawer_list([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.HOME, \"text\": \"Inbox\"}, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.STAR, \"text\": \"Starred\"}], 0, go_to)) var cart := GoFab.make(GoIconSet.PLUS, \"Add to cart\", add_to_cart) cart.float_in(self, nav.get_combined_minimum_size().y) var search := GoSearchBar.make(\"Search products\", find) search.add_action(GoIconSet.FILTER, &\"Filter\", open_filters) var send := GoSplitButton.make(\"Send\", send_now, [\"Send later\", \"Save as draft\"]) send.chosen.connect(func(index: int) -> void: send_variant(index)) var tabs := GoTabView.make([\"Posts\", \"Photos\", \"Saved\"], [posts, photos, saved]) tabs.tab_changed.connect(func(index: int) -> void: track_tab(index)) var row := GoStyle.tabs([\"Overview\", \"Stats\", \"Gear\"], 0, false, true) row.tab_changed.connect(show_panel) screen.set_bottom_bar(GoStyle.bottom_app_bar([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.SEARCH, \"tooltip\": &\"search\"}, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.HEART, \"tooltip\": &\"Like\"}], GoFab.make(GoIconSet.PLUS))) page.add_child(GoStyle.toolbar([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.EDIT, \"tooltip\": &\"Edit\", \"action\": edit}, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.TRASH, \"tooltip\": &\"Delete\", \"action\": delete}])) page.add_child(GoStyle.breadcrumb([\"Home\", \"Shop\", \"Swords\"], go_to_level)) var pages := GoPagination.make(1, 12, load_page) page.add_child(pages) var banners := GoCarousel.new() banners.set_pages([promo, event, pack])",-1],[4,"buttons","Buttons, chips and choices (9)",0,"GoStyle.button Buttons in seven tones: normal, primary, outlined, text, compact, danger and filled danger. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.glow Raises a filled button with a glow. a function of GoStyle GoIconButton An icon-only button: small to see, 48dp to touch, named for screen readers. extends Button GoStyle.chip A status or tag pill whose text always reads. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.filter_chip · input_chip A chip that toggles, and an entered value with a ✕. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.segmented Exactly one of a few options, joined in a row. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.choice_grid Pick one swatch — a colour, a skin — from a grid. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.radio_group Radio buttons, one of which is chosen. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.toggle · checkbox A switch and a check box with their labels. a function of GoStyle","row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Play\", play, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Details\", open_details, GoStyle.Tone.OUTLINED)) row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Skip\", skip, GoStyle.Tone.BARE)) row.add_child(GoStyle.glow(GoStyle.button(\"Play\", play, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY))) row.add_child(GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.CLOSE, close, -1, &\"close\")) var bell := GoIconButton.new() bell.icon_name = GoIconSet.BELL row.add_child(GoStyle.chip(\"Rare\", GoUi.color(GoTheme.INFO))) filters.add_child(GoStyle.filter_chip(\"In stock\", false, refilter)) to.add_child(GoStyle.input_chip(\"Ann\", remove_ann, GoIconSet.USER)) page.add_child(GoStyle.segmented([\"Day\", \"Week\", \"Month\"], 0, show_range)) var skins := GoStyle.choice_grid([{\"color\": \"f6cfae\", \"tooltip\": \"Peach\"}, {\"color\": \"8d5a36\", \"tooltip\": \"Cocoa\"}], 0, pick_skin) page.add_child(GoStyle.radio_group([\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\"], 1)) var music := GoStyle.toggle(\"Music\", false) var terms := GoStyle.checkbox(\"I agree to the terms\", false)",-1],[4,"inputs","Inputs and pickers (12)",0,"GoStyle.line_edit · textarea A one-line and a multi-line text field. a function of GoStyle GoField Label, control and hint, with an error under the field that is wrong. extends VBoxContainer GoInputGroup An input and its buttons welded into one shape. extends HBoxContainer GoCombobox A picker that searches inside names, not just from their start. extends Button GoCodeInput Coupon and gift codes as cells; paste and IME input keep working. extends VBoxContainer GoStyle.select · dropdown A drop-down list, and a button that opens a menu. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.slider A slider in the theme's shape. a function of GoStyle GoRangeSlider Two handles that never cross — a price or a level range. extends Control GoDatePicker A month to tap; a range of days with range_mode. extends Container GoTimePicker The clock dial: the hour, then the minutes; 12 or 24 hours; Up and Down on a box. extends Container GoWheelPicker A wheel that spins and settles one item on its band. extends Control GoStepper Numbered steps with Next and Back, down the page or in a row. extends VBoxContainer","var nickname := GoStyle.line_edit(\"Your name\") var note := GoStyle.textarea(\"Message\", 4) var field := GoField.make(\"Nickname\", GoStyle.line_edit(), \"3–12 letters\", false) field.set_error(\"That name is taken\") var chat := GoInputGroup.make(GoStyle.line_edit(\"Message\"), {\"suffix\": GoStyle.button(\"Send\", send)}) var friend := GoCombobox.make(friends, -1, \"Find a friend\") friend.picked.connect(invite) var coupon := GoCodeInput.make(12, 4) coupon.completed.connect(redeem) var quality := GoStyle.select([\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\"]) var sort := GoStyle.dropdown(\"Sort\", [\"Newest\", \"Price\"], sort_by) var volume := GoStyle.slider(0.0, 1.0, 0.05) volume.value_changed.connect(set_volume) var price := GoRangeSlider.make(0.0, 500.0, 40.0, 220.0, 10.0) price.change_ended.connect(func(low: float, high: float) -> void: refilter(low, high)) var stay := GoDatePicker.make() stay.range_mode = true stay.range_picked.connect(func(start: Dictionary, end: Dictionary) -> void: book(start, end)) var alarm := GoTimePicker.make(7, 30, func(hour: int, minute: int) -> void: set_alarm(hour, minute)) alarm.use_24h = true var amount := GoWheelPicker.make([\"x1\", \"x5\", \"x10\", \"x50\"], 0, set_amount) row.add_child(amount) var checkout := GoStepper.make([{\"title\": \"Cart\", \"content\": cart}, {\"title\": \"Pay\", \"content\": pay}]) checkout.finished.connect(place_order)",-1],[4,"lists","Lists, cards and data (8)",0,"GoStyle.list_row · list_button A list row with an icon, a title, a summary and a trailing mark. a function of GoStyle GoListView Thousands of rows; only the ones in view are built. extends GoScroll GoReorderList Rows you drag into order by a grip or a long press. extends Container GoSwipeRow A row you swipe aside to delete or archive; the list still scrolls. extends Container GoTable Sortable headers and selectable rows; numbers sort as numbers. extends VBoxContainer GoStyle.card · item_card A card, and the detail card of a picked item. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.avatar Initials or a picture in a disc. a function of GoStyle GoStyle.label Text in one of seven type roles, from micro to title. a function of GoStyle","page.add_child(GoStyle.list_button(GoIconSet.SETTINGS, \"Settings\", open_settings, Color.TRANSPARENT, \"\", false)) var feed := GoListView.make(10000, 72.0, func(index: int) -> Control: return post_row(posts[index])) feed.end_reached.connect(load_more) var queue := GoReorderList.make([intro_row, theme_row, boss_row]) queue.reordered.connect(func(from: int, to: int) -> void: songs.insert(to, songs.pop_at(from))) inbox.add_child(GoSwipeRow.wrap(mail_row, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.TRASH, \"text\": \"Delete\", \"tone\": GoTheme.DANGER, \"action\": delete_mail})) var board := GoTable.make([\"Name\", {\"text\": \"Score\", \"numeric\": true}], [[\"Ann\", 9124], [\"Ben\", 91240]]) board.row_selected.connect(open_profile) var card := GoStyle.card() card.add_child(GoStyle.label(\"Daily quest\")) popup.add_child(GoStyle.item_card({\"title\": \"Rusty sword\", \"subtitle\": \"Common\"})) row.add_child(GoStyle.avatar(\"AK\", 40)) page.add_child(GoStyle.label(\"Level 12\", GoTheme.ROLE_TITLE)) page.add_child(GoStyle.label(\"Next level in 340 XP\", GoTheme.ROLE_CAPTION, GoUi.color(GoTheme.MUTED)))",-1],[4,"hud","HUD and game shapes (11)",0,"GoBar HP, MP and XP bars with a value, a fraction or a percent. extends Control GoSlot A quick slot: icon, quantity, cooldown and shortcut on one face. extends Button GoSlotGrid An inventory grid; items can be dragged between cells. extends HFlowContainer GoJoystick A virtual stick — fixed, following the thumb, or relative. extends Control GoKbd Key caps that read the real binding, so rebinding never makes the hint lie. extends HBoxContainer GoChoiceColumn A short column of choices tapped once — a summon list; the game marks any number of rows. extends Control GoRewardCalendar Daily attendance rewards; only today can be pressed. extends VBoxContainer GoRadar The stat pentagon, with a dashed line to compare gear. extends Control GoDonut Shares as slices, with a legend in words as well as colour. extends Control GoZoomView Pinch, wheel and double tap to zoom a map; pans inside its edges. extends Control GoStyle.hud_panel · overlay_panel Panels that float over the game, so text stays readable on any picture. a function of GoStyle","var hp := GoBar.new() hp.label_text = \"HP\" hp.set_values(320, 500) var potion := GoSlot.new() potion.icon_name = GoIconSet.POTION potion.quantity = 12 potion.start_cooldown(5.0) var bag := GoSlotGrid.new() bag.set_cell(0, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.POTION, \"quantity\": 12}) var pad := GoJoystick.new() pad.mode = GoJoystick.Mode.FOLLOW pad.moved.connect(func(direction: Vector2) -> void: player.move(direction)) hint.add_child(GoKbd.for_action(&\"interact\")) var animals := GoChoiceColumn.make([\"Hen\", \"Cat\", \"Dog\", \"Pig\", \"Cow\"], 4, summon) animals.set_selected(2, true) side_bar.add_center(animals) var attendance := GoRewardCalendar.make(days, claimed_until) attendance.claimed.connect(func(day: int) -> void: server.claim_day(day)) var stats := GoRadar.make({\"STR\": 0.85, \"AGI\": 0.5, \"INT\": 0.3, \"VIT\": 0.7, \"LUK\": 0.45}) stats.set_compare(with_new_sword) var share := GoDonut.make([{\"label\": \"Physical\", \"value\": 620}, {\"label\": \"Magic\", \"value\": 340}]) card.add_child(share.legend()) var map := GoZoomView.wrap(world_map, 4.0) map.custom_minimum_size.y = 320 page.add_child(map) var bars := GoStyle.hud_panel() var pill := GoStyle.overlay_panel()",-1],[4,"look","Looks and system (8)",0,"GoUi · GoThemePresets Pick a preset — default, sci-fi, medieval, Material, kids, comic or arcade; read colours and sizes from the tokens. extends RefCounted GoConfig One resource for every setting, which survives add-on updates. extends Resource GoSkin The shapes code draws — chips, slots, the joystick, the new parts — in your own style. extends Resource GoIconSet · GoGameIcons Icons by name: the default set, 187 game icons, or your own SVGs. extends Resource · RefCounted GoStyleBoxCut · GoStyleBoxBracket · GoStyleBoxMedieval Chamfered, bracketed and forged faces for your own panels. extends StyleBox GoSafeArea · GoScale Notches, the gesture bar and the keyboard; breakpoints in dp. extends Control · RefCounted GoFeedback Sound cues and haptics routed to your own audio; gohud ships no sound. extends RefCounted GoBackPolicy Who owns Android Back and Escape right now, shared across windows. extends RefCounted","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MATERIAL_LIGHT) var accent := GoUi.color(GoTheme.ACCENT) var gap := GoUi.metric(GoTheme.GAP) GoUi.config.reduce_motion = true GoUi.config.container_alpha = 1.0 GoUi.refresh() class_name MySkin extends GoSkin func banner_box() -> StyleBox: return surface_box(GoTheme.BOX_CARD) GoUi.config.icons = GoGameIcons.icon_set() var gear := GoUi.icons().node(GoIconSet.SETTINGS, 24) var face := GoStyleBoxCut.new() face.cut = 8 panel.add_theme_stylebox_override(&\"panel\", face) var usable := GoSafeArea.usable_rect(get_window()) var size_class := GoScale.breakpoint_for_dp(minf(usable.size.x, usable.size.y)) # by the short side GoFeedback.sound_handler = func(cue: String) -> void: audio.play_cue(cue) GoFeedback.haptic_handler = func(ms: int, amplitude: float) -> void: Input.vibrate_handheld(ms, amplitude) GoBackPolicy.acquire(get_tree())",-1],[5,"popup-map","Pick the right popup",0,"A popup interrupts. Before choosing one, answer a single question: must the player answer before the game goes on? If yes, block. If no, never block — a card that stops the game for news the player did not ask for is the fastest way to make them close your game. A question with an answer — buy, delete, leave, overwrite → GoDialogs.confirm(). Something to acknowledge → alert(). One of a few options → choose(). A screen of its own — settings, a character sheet, a shop item → GoSurface in the middle of the screen. A long list or a management page — the bag, mail, friends → GoSheet from the bottom on a phone, GoDrawer from the side on a wide screen. Something about the thing just pressed — an item's stats, its actions → GoPopover or GoContextMenu beside it. News the game can carry on through — saved, dropped, invited → GoSnackbar, GoNotice or GoPromptCard. These never take the screen. Teaching the controls → GoCoachMark. Cheats while you build → GoConsole.","",-1],[5,"every-popup-at-a-glance","Every popup at a glance",1,"Popup Stops the game Back / Escape A tap outside Use it for GoDialogs confirm · alert Yes Closes it — confirm answers false, alert returns Closes it only with dismiss_on_scrim Questions that need an answer GoDialogs.choose Yes Closes it — answers -1 Closes it only with dismiss_on_scrim Picking one of a few GoSurface Yes Asks to close the topmost Asks to close with dismiss_on_scrim Windows of your own GoSheet Yes Closes the whole sheet Closes it The bag, a shop list, mail GoDrawer Yes Android Back only Closes it A side list on a wide screen GoPopover Until it closes Closes it Closes it — and goes no further Item and skill details GoCombobox list Until it closes Closes it Closes it A pick list that searches GoContextMenu · dropdown · select The engine's menu The engine's menu Closes it Actions, short lists GoSnackbar No — Reaches the game Saved · Undo · Retry GoPromptCard No — Reaches the game An invite, a trade request GoNotice Never — Reaches the game A fixed line on the HUD GoBanner No — it is in the page — — \"You're offline. Retry\" GoCoachMark Its card only Ends the tour Reaches the game A first-run tour GoConsole Its panel only The Escape key closes it Reaches the game Debug commands Which layer each one opens on, and why in that order, is under Layers, Back and input. GoDialogs GoSurface GoSheet GoDrawer GoPopover GoContextMenu GoSnackbar GoPromptCard GoCoachMark GoConsole Every picture on this page is the same little game — health and mana top left, coins top right, a joystick and three quick slots at the bottom — in default_dark, with one popup open over it. The same popup in all fourteen looks →","",56],[5,"popup-anatomy","Anatomy of a popup",0,"Almost every blocking popup in gohud — dialogs, sheets, popovers, the combobox list and your own windows — is one node, GoSurface. Learn its parts once and you know all of them. Header with back and close · body · status line · footer Part What it is How you reach it Layer The CanvasLayer the popup lives on. Its number decides what it covers. Yours for a GoSurface; built in for the others (table) Scrim The veil over everything behind. It catches the taps that miss the card. scrim_transparent, dismiss_on_scrim, the theme's scrim colour Card The window itself — the theme's panel face, rounded, cut, forged or jelly depending on the look. card, alpha Header An optional back button, the title (two lines at most, then \"…\"), the close button. set_title() · set_title_key() · set_back() · close_enabled · show_header Toolbar A pinned row under the header — a search field, filter chips. Hidden until you use it. toolbar Body The scrolling part. Put the content here. body · scroll_body · clear() Status line A pinned line between the body and the footer — \"Name check failed\", \"Saving…\". set_status_text() · set_status_key() · clear_status() Footer Pinned buttons at the bottom. Hidden until you use it. footer Pinned things go in the pinned rows. A search field, an error or a Save button put in the body scrolls away with a long list — the player types a wrong name, the error is under the fold, and nothing seems to happen. Use toolbar, the status line and footer; they stay put while the body scrolls.","",-1],[5,"popup-dialogs","Dialogs you await",0,"GoDialogs asks and waits. One node, three questions — and the answer comes back on the same line, so the code reads in the order the player experiences it. confirm() confirm(…, true) — destructive alert() choose() ActionLayout.HORIZONTAL","var dialogs := GoDialogs.new() add_child(dialogs) if await dialogs.confirm(\"Buy the starter pack?\", \"300 gems for a sword, a shield and 10 potions.\", \"Buy\", \"Not now\"): buy_starter_pack()",-1],[5,"the-three-questions","The three questions",1,"Call Returns Use it for confirm() true or false Yes or no — buy, delete, leave, overwrite. alert() nothing — await it to wait Something the player must see: a reward, a lost connection. choose() the option's index, or -1 One of a few. An option is a String or {text, icon, danger, subtitle}. confirm_key() · alert_key() as above The same with translation keys — the words follow a language change while the dialog is open. Empty button labels fall back to the kit's own words (confirm, cancel in GoConfig.text_keys). extra is added to the body on a new line. args fills {placeholders} in the title and the body: confirm(\"Buy {item}?\", \"It costs {price} gold.\", \"Buy\", \"\", \"\", {\"item\": name, \"price\": 300}).","confirm(title, body, ok_text := \"\", cancel_text := \"\", extra := \"\", args := {}, destructive := false) -> bool alert(title, body, ok_text := \"\", extra := \"\", args := {}) # await it to wait choose(title, options: Array, cancel_text := \"\", translate := false) -> int confirm_key(…) · alert_key(…) # translation keys",59],[5,"every-way-out-has-an-answer","Every way out has an answer",1,"The player… confirm alert choose presses OK / an option true returns the option's index presses Cancel false — -1 presses ×, Escape or Android Back false returns -1 taps the scrim (only with dismiss_on_scrim) false returns -1 the GoDialogs node leaves the tree false returns -1 So code after await always runs — no answer is ever left hanging, even when the scene changes under the dialog.","",59],[5,"destructive-actions","Destructive actions",1,"Pass destructive = true for something that cannot be undone. The OK button becomes the filled Tone.DANGER_SOLID button — white on red in every look, where a tinted danger label would have to darken to near-black on a light theme to stay legible. The tone is reset on every call, because the window is reused. OK has the keyboard focus. Every confirmation opens with its OK button focused, so Enter or Space confirms — a destructive one too. Word the buttons so the safe choice is obvious (\"Keep it\"), and keep irreversible actions behind a second step when a slip costs the player real progress.","if await dialogs.confirm(\"Delete this save?\", \"Slot 2 — Aria, level 12. This cannot be undone.\", \"Delete\", \"Keep it\", \"\", {}, true): delete_save(2)",59],[5,"button-layout","Button layout",1,"action_layout What it does VERTICAL (default) Buttons stacked, full width. Safe for every language — a long German or Russian label never squeezes. HORIZONTAL One row, half the width each. AUTO One row only when both labels fit half the card on a single line; stacked otherwise. Decided again on a language change or a resize. action_gap is the space between the buttons, body_gap the space above them — make it wider than the button gap so the question and the choice read as two parts. For one dialog only, call set_next_action_layout() before opening it. An alert's single button always takes the full width.","",59],[5,"one-at-a-time","One at a time",1,"A second confirm() while one is open returns false at once — a dialog never stacks on a dialog by accident. Turn on queue_when_busy and it waits its turn instead; alert() always waits. queue_limit (8) caps the line, and on overflow the oldest request is answered false. pending() counts the waiting requests and clear_pending() answers them all false. choose() never queues: it returns -1 when a dialog is already open.","",59],[5,"phone-and-desktop","Phone and desktop",1,"choose() opens as a sheet from the bottom on Android and iOS — where the thumb is — and as a card in the middle on a desktop. A confirm is capped at max_width (420dp) and centred. Set layer_index, max_width and the other exports before add_child; they are applied when the node enters the tree.","var picked := await dialogs.choose(\"Sort the bag by\", [ {\"text\": \"Newest first\", \"icon\": GoIconSet.CLOCK}, {\"text\": \"Rarity\", \"icon\": GoIconSet.STAR}, {\"text\": \"Drop everything\", \"icon\": GoIconSet.TRASH, \"danger\": true}]) if picked >= 0: sort_bag(picked)",59],[5,"popup-surface","GoSurface — a window of your own",0,"When a popup is more than a question — settings, a character sheet, an item to buy — build it on GoSurface. The safe area, the keyboard, pinned rows, scrolling, Back, focus and resizing are done. It never closes itself. × , Escape, Back and a scrim tap only emit close_requested. Hiding or freeing the window is the owning screen's job — only it knows whether \"close\" means save, discard or ask first.","var layer := CanvasLayer.new() layer.layer = 50 add_child(layer) var window := GoSurface.new() window.set_title(\"Settings\") window.close_requested.connect(layer.queue_free) window.body.add_child(GoStyle.toggle(\"Music\", false)) window.body.add_child(GoStyle.slider(0.0, 1.0, 0.05)) var row := GoStyle.row() row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Cancel\", window.request_close)) row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Save\", save_and_close, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) window.footer.add_child(row) window.footer.visible = true layer.add_child(window)",-1],[5,"three-placements","Three placements",1,"CENTER — confirmations, settings BOTTOM — lists, management pages ANCHOR — beside a control A GoDatePicker in a CENTER window ANCHOR needs anchor_control. The card goes to the right of it if anchor_min_width fits, otherwise to the wider side, otherwise inside the screen, and opens upward when there is more room above. It follows a moving anchor every frame. anchor_width (320) and anchor_max_height (520) size it.","",66],[5,"how-big-it-gets","How big it gets",1,"Measure Rule Change it with Room The safe area, minus the keyboard, minus the screen margin (16dp, never more than 10% of the short side). — Width 94% of the room in portrait, 72% in landscape, at most 480dp. max_width · GoConfig.surface_width_ratio_* Height As tall as the content (fit_content), up to 68% of the room, capped at 72%. A centred card that is not resizable may grow to 94% to avoid scrolling. height_ratio · max_height_ratio · max_height Density Dense when compact is set, the screen is under 420dp tall (a phone on its side), or the content does not fit: less padding, smaller gaps, a smaller title. It measures both and keeps the roomier one that fits — no jitter. compact Resize With resizable, the title is a handle: drag it between 30% and the cap. height_changed(ratio) reports the result. resizable A ratio above the cap is cut back, with one warning in a debug build. The keyboard pushes the card up and scrolls the focused field into view; the safe area keeps it off the notch and the gesture bar on Android and iOS.","",66],[5,"properties","Properties",1,"Property Default What it does placement CENTER CENTER, BOTTOM or ANCHOR dismiss_on_scrim GoConfig.dismiss_on_scrim (false) A tap on the scrim asks to close. A drag that started inside the card does not. scrim_transparent false Keep the game visible — the scrim still catches outside taps. close_enabled true Show × and let Escape and Back ask to close. show_header · scroll_body · resizable true · true · false The header row, the scrolling body, the drag handle. fit_content · compact true · false Size to the content; start dense. fade_in GoConfig.surface_fade_in (false) Fade the card in when it opens. Instant under reduce_motion. alpha -1 (the theme's) The card face's opacity, as a ratio. Only the face fades — never the text. initial_focus none The control focused on open. Set these before add_child: scrim_transparent, show_header, resizable and scroll_body are applied when the window enters the tree. dismiss_on_scrim, close_enabled, fade_in and initial_focus are read live.","",66],[5,"signals-and-calls","Signals and calls",1,"Name What it is close_requested ×, Escape, Android Back or a scrim tap — and request_close(). Emitted only by the topmost window. back_requested · set_back(action) The header's back button, for a window with pages. An empty Callable hides it. height_changed(ratio) After a drag on the handle. is_top() · GoSurface.is_any_open() Is this the window that takes Back — is any window open at all. relayout() Lay out again now. Changing a sizing property already does it for you.","",66],[5,"popup-sheets","Sheets and drawers",0,"A list that needs room comes up from the bottom on a phone held upright — where the thumb is — and in from the side on a tablet or a desktop, where a sheet would cover the game. GoSheet GoDrawer · LEFT GoDrawer · RIGHT","",-1],[5,"gosheet-pages-from-the-bottom","GoSheet — pages from the bottom",1,"It is a CanvasLayer (layer 10) holding a BOTTOM, resizable GoSurface — so it sits above the HUD, and the player can drag it taller. open(title) starts a fresh page: it clears the body, the toolbar and the back button and frees what add_footer() added. Call it again to show another page in the same sheet; set_back() shows a back button for the way home. open_key() takes a translation key. close() hides it — it is not freed, so the next open() is instant. closed and page_changed tell you when. height_ratio (0.6) is the height it opens at; max_height_ratio lifts the cap; dismissable (true) closes it on a scrim tap. Escape and Back close the whole sheet, even on a sub-page with set_back() — only the on-screen back button walks back a page. If Back should step back, handle close_requested on sheet.surface yourself.","var sheet := GoSheet.new() add_child(sheet) func show_bag(items: Array) -> void: sheet.open(\"Bag\") var search := GoStyle.line_edit(\"Search the bag…\") search.text_changed.connect(filter_bag) sheet.toolbar().add_child(search) sheet.toolbar().visible = true for item in items: sheet.body.add_child(GoStyle.list_button(GoIconSet.BOX, item.name, show_item.bind(item), Color.TRANSPARENT, item.description, false, GoIconSet.CHEVRON_RIGHT)) sheet.add_footer(GoStyle.button(\"Close\", sheet.close, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY))",71],[5,"godrawer-from-the-side","GoDrawer — from the side",1,"Layer 80. 42% of the screen wide (width_ratio), between min_width (320dp) and max_width (420dp) — on a phone it covers most of the screen, which is why a sheet is the better choice there. The panel reaches the screen edge; only its content steps in from the safe area, so a rounded corner never clips the first row. LEFT means screen-left even in Arabic. Turn on follow_text_direction when \"the start side\" is the point; effective_side() tells you where it went. open(title) keeps the body — fill it once. set_title(\"\") hides the header. motion_seconds (0.2) slides it; reduce_motion makes it instant. Android Back closes a drawer; Escape does not. The drawer listens for the system Back only. On a desktop, call drawer.close() from your own key binding — and note that GoSurface.is_any_open() does not count a drawer; ask drawer.is_open().","var drawer := GoDrawer.new() drawer.side = GoDrawer.Side.LEFT drawer.follow_text_direction = true # the start side: left, or right in Arabic add_child(drawer) drawer.body.add_child(GoNavBar.drawer_list([{\"icon\": GoIconSet.HOME, \"text\": \"Town\"}, {\"icon\": GoIconSet.MAP, \"text\": \"World map\"}], 0, go_to)) drawer.open(\"Menu\")",71],[5,"popup-anchored","Cards and menus beside a control",0,"What the player just pressed deserves an answer right next to the finger, not in the middle of the screen. GoPopover GoContextMenu GoStyle.dropdown() GoStyle.select() GoCombobox","",-1],[5,"gopopover-a-card-on-the-thing-pressed","GoPopover — a card on the thing pressed",1,"An ANCHOR surface with the layer, the anchor and the teardown already wired — the ten lines every game writes again and again. One at a time: opening a second closes the first, because stacked cards bury the screen and nobody can tell which belongs to which slot. The scrim is transparent — a card opened to compare gear must not darken the gear — but it still catches the first outside tap, which closes the card and goes no further. Option Default What it does title \"\" A header with ×. Empty means no header. width · max_height 320 · 520 The card's size. dismissable true An outside tap closes it. compact · alpha · translate false · -1 · false Dense spacing, face opacity, title as a translation key. layer 95 The CanvasLayer it opens on. GoPopover.close() and GoPopover.is_open() are static. open() returns the surface — or null when the anchor is not in the tree, so check before you await shown.close_requested. It is not a hover tooltip. Touch has no hover; anything only a mouse can reveal is invisible to half your players. And with dismissable = false and no title, nothing on screen closes it — only Escape, Back or your own call.","slot.pressed.connect(func() -> void: var card := GoStyle.item_card({\"icon\": GoIconSet.POTION, \"title\": \"Health potion\", \"subtitle\": \"Heals 50 HP · 12 left\"}, false) GoPopover.open(slot, card, {\"width\": 280}))",74],[5,"gocontextmenu-long-press-and-right-click","GoContextMenu — long-press and right-click",1,"A right-click opens it at once. A finger held for half a second (HOLD_SECONDS) opens it; moving more than 12dp cancels — so scrolling a list never pops a menu. An item is {text, action, icon, disabled, checked, separator, danger, translate}. Pass a Callable instead of the array when the entries depend on what was pressed; it is called each time the menu opens. danger puts \"⚠ \" before the text — the engine's menu can colour only all of its items at once. It is the engine's PopupMenu, dressed by GoStyle.style_popup(). It does not count as an open surface. A long press needs a second way in. Nobody finds a hidden gesture. Pair it with a visible ⋯ button (open_at(), as above), or teach it once with a coach mark.","var menu := [ {\"text\": \"Use\", \"icon\": GoIconSet.POTION, \"action\": use}, {\"separator\": true}, {\"text\": \"Drop\", \"icon\": GoIconSet.TRASH, \"action\": drop, \"danger\": true}] GoContextMenu.attach(slot, menu) var more := GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.MORE, Callable(), -1, &\"more\") more.pressed.connect(func() -> void: GoContextMenu.open_at(more, menu))",74],[5,"dropdowns-selects-and-the-split-button","Dropdowns, selects and the split button",1,"All three open the engine's popup menu: dropdown() is a MenuButton that runs an action, select() an OptionButton that keeps a value, GoSplitButton a main action plus a menu on its arrow (chosen(index)). Menus stay fully opaque on purpose — a menu shown in its own OS window turns translucent pixels black.","var sort := GoStyle.dropdown(\"Sort\", [\"Highest score\", \"Most wins\", {\"text\": \"Friends only\", \"disabled\": true}], func(index: int) -> void: sort_board(index)) var quality := GoStyle.select([\"Low\", \"Medium\", \"High\", \"Ultra\"], \"Quality\") quality.item_selected.connect(func(index: int) -> void: settings.quality = index) var send := GoSplitButton.make(\"Send\", send_now, [\"Send later\", \"Save as draft\"])",74],[5,"gocombobox-a-list-that-searches","GoCombobox — a list that searches",1,"Pressed, it opens an anchored list on layer 96 with a transparent scrim. From search_threshold (8) entries a search field appears and takes the focus; it matches anywhere in the text or the hint, ignoring case, and an empty result says so. list_width (0 = the button's width, at least 180dp) sizes the list.","var friend := GoCombobox.make(friend_names, -1, \"Find a friend\") friend.picked.connect(func(index: int) -> void: invite(friend_names[index]))",74],[5,"popup-nonblocking","Popups that never stop the game",0,"News the player can read while playing. None of these has a scrim; a tap anywhere but the card itself goes to the game. GoSnackbar GoNotice GoPromptCard GoStyle.tooltip_node()","",-1],[5,"gosnackbar-a-message-with-an-undo","GoSnackbar — a message with an Undo",1,"Key of post() What it does text · title · args · translate The message, an optional bold line, {placeholders}, translation keys. tone · icon The accent colour (GoTheme.SUCCESS, WARNING…) and an icon. actions · closable Buttons — Strings or {text, action} — and an ×. seconds How long it stays. Negative: the theme's notice_duration_ms. 0: until dismissed — give it a button then. post() returns the index of the button pressed, or -1 when it timed out or was dismissed. Posts queue (queue_limit 4, the oldest dropped with -1), and the same text posted again while it shows only refills its timer. It sits at the bottom (or the top, placement), above the safe area and the keyboard, on layer 90 — readable over a drawer. With tap_to_dismiss (on) a tap on a card without buttons closes it; a tap off the card always reaches the game. show_text() and show_key() are the one-line forms. Never ask a question in a snackbar. It goes away on its own; a choice that matters belongs in a dialog.","var snack := GoSnackbar.new() add_child(snack) if await snack.post({\"text\": \"Dropped {name}\", \"args\": {\"name\": item.name}, \"icon\": GoIconSet.TRASH, \"actions\": [\"Undo\"], \"seconds\": 5.0}) == 0: restore(item)",79],[5,"gonotice-a-line-on-the-hud","GoNotice — a line on the HUD",1,"A plain panel you place yourself — in a GoHudAnchor, in a corner, anywhere. It takes neither input nor focus, so pressing through it reaches the button underneath, and a new message replaces the old one. Give it a width: preferred_width(limit) returns the natural width of short text and wraps long text within limit. set_content() shows any control instead of text.","var notice := GoNotice.new() hud_corner.add_child(notice) notice.show_text(\"Game saved\", GoTheme.SUCCESS) notice.custom_minimum_size.x = notice.preferred_width(340)",79],[5,"gopromptcard-a-question-that-can-wait","GoPromptCard — a question that can wait",1,"It starts hidden — call show(). It has no timer of its own; add one if the question expires. Its buttons do not close it — the actions decide. × (set_closable(true)) emits closed. fit_width(width) sets the width and predicts the height from the font, so nothing laid out against it jumps a frame later. Its face follows hud_alpha — it is part of the HUD, not a window.","var spot := GoHudAnchor.new() spot.spot = GoHudAnchor.Spot.TOP_CENTER spot.reserve_space = false spot.avoid_peers = true # step below the health bars instead of covering them hud.add_child(spot) var invite := GoPromptCard.new() spot.add_child(invite) invite.set_icon(GoIconSet.USERS, Color.TRANSPARENT, true) invite.set_title(\"Party invite from Ann\") invite.set_subtitle(\"Dragon's Lair · 3 / 4 members\") invite.set_actions([{\"text\": \"Accept\", \"action\": accept, \"primary\": true}, {\"text\": \"Decline\", \"action\": invite.hide}]) invite.fit_width(340) invite.show() get_tree().create_timer(15.0).timeout.connect(invite.hide)",79],[5,"gobanner-and-tooltips","GoBanner and tooltips",1,"GoBanner.make(\"You're offline.\", [{\"text\": \"Retry\", \"action\": reconnect}], GoIconSet.WARNING) sits in the page itself, above the content, and never times out; a button dismisses it unless it has \"keep\": true. GoStyle.tooltip_node(text) is what to return from _make_custom_tooltip() — the engine draws the plate (TooltipPanel), gohud the text, wrapped past 260dp. Tooltips are for a mouse; never hide what a player needs behind one.","",79],[5,"popup-guides","Tours and the console",0,"GoCoachMark GoConsole","",-1],[5,"gocoachmark-a-tour-of-the-real-controls","GoCoachMark — a tour of the real controls",1,"A ring around the real control and a card beside it. Pressing the target advances (its pressed signal, or \"signal\" in the step); Next and Skip are on the card. A hidden target is skipped. The card stays out of the middle of the screen (avoid_center_band), off the HUD anchors and off keep_clear. While any GoSurface is open the tour hides and waits. Back or Escape ends it with finished(false). It has no layer of its own — add it last, or on a layer above the HUD.","var tour := GoCoachMark.new() tour.keep_clear = [top_bar] tour_layer.add_child(tour) tour.finished.connect(func(completed: bool) -> void: save.tutorial_done = true) tour.start([{\"target\": bag_button, \"title\": \"Bag\", \"body\": \"Everything you pick up lands here.\"}, {\"target\": map_button, \"title\": \"Map\", \"body\": \"Tap to open the full map.\"}])",84],[5,"goconsole-cheats-while-you-build","GoConsole — cheats while you build",1,"Layer 200 — above everything, so you can debug over a dialog — and it keeps running while the tree is paused. A palette suggests commands as you type; Up and Down walk the history; Escape closes it. There is no built-in key: bind your own. debug_only (on) blocks it in a release build — both open() and run(). Cheat commands in a player's hands end a game's economy on the first day.","var console := GoConsole.new() add_child(console) console.register(\"give\", \"give <item> <count>\", func(args: PackedStringArray) -> String: return \"gave %s x%s\" % [args[0], args[1]] if args.size() >= 2 else \"give <item> <count>\") func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void: if event.is_action_pressed(&\"dev_console\"): console.toggle()",84],[5,"popup-stack","Layers, Back and input",0,"Three rules decide what the player can touch while something is open: what is on top, who owns Back, and who takes a tap.","",-1],[5,"what-sits-on-top","What sits on top",1,"Layer What sits there Set with 5 Your HUD (your choice) — 10 GoSheet CanvasLayer.layer ~50 Your own GoSurface windows, a pause menu your CanvasLayer 80 GoDrawer CanvasLayer.layer 90 GoSnackbar layer_index 95 GoPopover \"layer\" option 96 GoCombobox list — 100 GoDialogs layer_index 200 GoConsole layer_index The order is deliberate: a snackbar reports what just happened, so it reads over a drawer; a popover belongs to what was just pressed, so it sits above that; a dialog asks a question and covers both; the console covers everything, because it is what you open when the rest has gone wrong.","",87],[5,"who-owns-back","Who owns Back",1,"Only the topmost window answers. Among the open surfaces, the one on the highest layer (then the latest in the tree) takes Escape, gamepad cancel (ui_cancel), Android Back and scrim taps. Stacked windows close one at a time, never together. Android Back is handled one frame later, so one press can never close two windows. While anything that owns Back is open, Android Back does not quit the app (GoBackPolicy counts the owners and restores quit_on_go_back after the last one). Your own popup that takes Back should call GoBackPolicy.acquire() and release() — in _exit_tree too. A drawer, a coach-mark tour and a form step aside while a surface is open — Back goes to the surface first. GoConfig.close_on_back (on) is the switch for surfaces.","",87],[5,"who-takes-a-tap","Who takes a tap",1,"A surface covers the whole screen and stops input — a transparent scrim too. Nothing on a lower layer is pressed while it is open; layers above it (a snackbar) still are. Mouse-wheel and pinch gestures stop at the window as well: scrolling past the end of a list never scrolls the game. Gameplay input that does not go through controls — _unhandled_input for movement, a camera drag — should pause: if GoSurface.is_any_open(): return. That covers dialogs, sheets, popovers and the combobox; ask a drawer is_open() separately. Snackbar, notice, prompt card and coach mark take input only on their own card; everywhere else, the game gets it.","",87],[5,"focus","Focus",1,"A window opened by a pointer focuses nothing — no ring flashes for a touch. Opened from a keyboard or gamepad, the close button (or initial_focus) takes focus. Focus stays inside the window while it is open and goes back to the control that had it when the window closes. Dialogs focus OK every time.","",87],[5,"pausing-the-game","Pausing the game",1,"Pausing the tree pauses popups too — only the console keeps working. For a pause menu, give its layer process_mode = PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS; then the window, its buttons and Back keep running while the game is stopped.","",87],[5,"popup-looks","The same popup in every look",0,"The confirmation from the top of this page, over the same game, with only the preset changed. The code is identical — the theme, the skin and the icons do the rest. default_dark default_light scifi_dark scifi_light medieval_dark medieval_light material_light New material_dark New kids_light New kids_dark New comic_light New comic_dark New arcade_light New arcade_dark New","",-1],[5,"what-each-look-changes","What each look changes",1,"Look The window Its head and buttons Default Rounded (18dp), a soft shadow, 80% opaque over the game A plain title and ×; primary buttons lift and sink Sci-fi Cut corners with a neon edge and glow, the edge tinted by the accent Bracket focus marks Medieval A forged frame — iron and leather, or parchment — with rivets and corner ornaments Titles in Cinzel Material 3 28dp corners, 24dp padding, fully opaque A 24sp headline in Roboto; pill buttons with a 40dp plate in a 48dp target Kids A jelly-candy card with a soft shadow, fully opaque A sunny title ribbon (mint at night), a round candy close button, buttons that squish when pressed Comic A bold ink outline and a hard shadow, fully opaque A yellow title caption, an inked round close button, buttons whose shadow goes when pressed Arcade A thick board — a coloured frame round a pale well — fully opaque A gold title banner with a white, ink-outlined title, a round red close key, painted keys that pop when pressed","",93],[5,"dress-a-popup-from-a-skin","Dress a popup from a skin",1,"A skin decides the parts a Theme cannot reach. These hooks are the ones popups call — override them in your own GoSkin subclass; by default they do nothing. Hook What it dresses title_plate_box() · title_plate_ink() · title_plate_min_size() A plate behind a window's title. The title centres on it and shrinks, down to the minimum size (15), to stay on one line. dress_close_button(button) The window's × — kids makes it a round candy, comic an inked disc, arcade a round red key. dress_title(label) The window's title label — arcade outlines its white title in ink. press_feedback(control) Runs the moment a finger lands on a button gohud made — kids squishes it, arcade pops it. floating_box() · notice_box() · drawer_box() · banner_box() · overlay_box() The faces of prompt cards and coach cards, snackbars and notices, the drawer, banners, the console. coach_ring_box() · draw_coach_pointer() The tour's ring and pointer.","",93],[5,"how-see-through","How see-through",1,"Each kind of popup follows its own opacity, so a HUD card can stay light while a dialog stays solid: windows, sheets, dialogs, popovers and the combobox follow panel_alpha; the drawer and coach card card_alpha; prompt cards and the console hud_alpha; snackbars and notices notice_alpha; menus popup_alpha. Material and kids make them all opaque; comic too, except prompt cards and the console at 92%, and arcade, except those two at 94%. Override one kind with GoConfig.container_alpha_overrides, all of them with container_alpha (a ratio — 0.95), or one window with its alpha. Only the face fades; text is never see-through. Opacity in detail →","",93],[5,"popup-config","Settings that shape every popup",0,"Fields of GoConfig (GoUi.config). A few are copied when a window is created, so set them before building the UI — or call GoUi.refresh() after changing them. Field Default What it does surface_max_width · surface_max_height 480 · 700 The largest a window gets. surface_height_ratio · surface_max_height_ratio 0.68 · 0.72 The usual height and the cap (also the drag limit). surface_fit_max_height_ratio 0.94 How far a centred fit-content card may grow before it scrolls. surface_width_ratio_portrait · …_landscape 0.94 · 0.72 Width as a share of the room. dismiss_on_scrim false A scrim tap closes windows and dialogs. Copied when the window is created. surface_fade_in · fade_seconds false · 0.14 Fade windows in, and how fast. close_on_back true Escape, ui_cancel and Android Back close the topmost window. close_button_visual 36 How big × looks — its touch target stays 48dp. suppress_pointer_focus_ring true No focus ring when a window is opened by touch or mouse. container_alpha · container_alpha_overrides -1 · {} Opacity of every face, or per kind (GoTheme.BOX_*). reduce_motion false No fades, slides, pulses or squishes. min_touch_size 48 The height of prompt-card and coach-mark buttons. respect_safe_area true Keep windows off the notch and the gesture bar. text_keys · text_overrides — The kit's own words: close, back, confirm, cancel, next, done, skip, search, empty… sound_cues · haptics — What GoFeedback plays on opened, closed, confirmed, canceled and tapped.","",-1],[5,"popup-recipes","Recipes",0,"Copy, paste, change the words. Every call here is checked against the source.","",-1],[5,"a-purchase-with-the-price-in-it","A purchase with the price in it",1,"","func buy(item_name: String, price: int) -> void: if await dialogs.confirm(\"Buy {item}?\", \"It costs {price} gold.\", \"Buy\", \"\", \"\", {\"item\": item_name, \"price\": price}): purchase(item_name)",98],[5,"a-settings-window-with-a-pinned-save","A settings window with a pinned Save",1,"","func open_settings() -> void: var layer := CanvasLayer.new() layer.layer = 50 add_child(layer) var window := GoSurface.new() window.set_title(\"Settings\") window.dismiss_on_scrim = true window.close_requested.connect(layer.queue_free) window.body.add_child(GoStyle.section(\"Sound\", false)) window.body.add_child(GoStyle.toggle(\"Music\", false)) window.body.add_child(GoStyle.slider(0.0, 1.0, 0.05)) var row := GoStyle.row() row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Cancel\", window.request_close)) row.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Save\", func() -> void: save_settings() layer.queue_free(), GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) window.footer.add_child(row) window.footer.visible = true layer.add_child(window)",98],[5,"a-form-that-says-what-is-wrong","A form that says what is wrong",1,"","var field := GoField.make(\"Name\", GoStyle.line_edit(), \"3–12 letters\") window.body.add_child(field) create_button.pressed.connect(func() -> void: if name_is_taken(): field.set_error(\"That name is taken\") window.set_status_text(\"Name check failed\", GoTheme.DANGER) else: window.clear_status() create_character())",98],[5,"a-date-in-a-sheet","A date in a sheet",1,"","sheet.open(\"Delivery date\") var picker := GoDatePicker.make({\"year\": 2026, \"month\": 10, \"day\": 14}, func(date: Dictionary) -> void: delivery = date sheet.close()) picker.min_date = GoDatePicker.today() sheet.body.add_child(picker)",98],[5,"a-pause-menu","A pause menu",1,"","func pause() -> void: get_tree().paused = true var layer := CanvasLayer.new() layer.layer = 50 layer.process_mode = Node.PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS # keeps running while the game is paused add_child(layer) var menu := GoSurface.new() menu.set_title(\"Paused\") menu.close_requested.connect(func() -> void: get_tree().paused = false layer.queue_free()) menu.body.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Resume\", menu.request_close, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) menu.body.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Settings\", open_settings)) menu.body.add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Quit to title\", quit_to_title, GoStyle.Tone.DANGER)) layer.add_child(menu)",98],[5,"gameplay-that-waits-for-popups","Gameplay that waits for popups",1,"","func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void: if GoSurface.is_any_open() or drawer.is_open(): return handle_gameplay(event)",98],[5,"popup-pitfalls","Pitfalls",0,"A GoSurface never frees itself. Connect close_requested, or × does nothing. Options set after add_child — scrim_transparent, show_header, resizable, scroll_body, and GoDialogs' layer_index and max_width — are not applied. A second confirm() returns false at once. Turn on queue_when_busy if two questions can meet. Enter confirms. OK has the focus, on destructive dialogs too. Back on a sheet closes the sheet, not the sub-page. Escape does not close a drawer, and is_any_open() does not see one. A popover or combobox list blocks the game until it closes, even with a transparent scrim — and a popover with dismissable = false and no title has nothing on screen that closes it. A prompt card starts hidden and has no timeout. A snackbar with seconds: 0 and no button never leaves. And it catches taps on its card by default. A long press nobody knows about is a feature nobody uses. Show a ⋯ too. A paused tree pauses your popup. Use PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS on its layer. A notice without a width collapses to its narrowest — use preferred_width(). Never ask in a snackbar, never inform in a dialog. A question goes away when ignored; news should not stop the game.","",-1],[6,"gosurface-the-shell","GoSurface — the shell",1,"CENTER BOTTOM ANCHOR Popups, sheets and dropdowns all use this one. It handles the safe area, the virtual keyboard, sticky header and footer, a scrolling body, which window is topmost, focus restoration, back-button ownership and drag-to-resize. Placement Looks like Used for CENTER A card in the middle Confirmations, settings BOTTOM A sheet rising from below Lists, management pages ANCHOR A card pinned beside a control Dropdowns, context menus It does not remove itself. Reacting to close_requested — hiding or freeing — is the owning screen's job, because the shell cannot know why it is closing (save and close, or discard).","",-1],[6,"gosheet-a-page-from-the-bottom","GoSheet — a page from the bottom",1,"GoSheet It owns a CanvasLayer, so it reliably sits above the HUD. open() clears the body and turns off the back button and sticky rows — a dead button on a screen with nowhere to go back to reads as broken.","var sheet := GoSheet.new() add_child(sheet) sheet.open(\"Inventory\") sheet.toolbar().add_child(GoStyle.line_edit(\"Search…\")) sheet.toolbar().visible = true sheet.footer().add_child(GoStyle.button(\"Close\", sheet.close, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY)) sheet.footer().visible = true",-1],[6,"godialogs-confirmations-you-await","GoDialogs — confirmations you await",1,"confirm() destructive choose() confirm(title, body, ok_text, cancel_text, extra, args, destructive) — everything after the body is optional, and alert() works the same way with a single button. Set destructive for something that cannot be undone: the confirm button becomes the filled GoStyle.Tone.DANGER_SOLID button. On a light theme a tinted danger label has to darken until it reads as black text; the filled button keeps white text on red. The tone is re-applied on every call because one window is reused, and a second confirm() while one is open returns false at once. confirm_key() takes translation keys. Button layout. action_layout is VERTICAL by default (safe for long translations), HORIZONTAL for one row with half the width each, or AUTO, which uses one row only when both labels fit half the card on a single line and stacks them otherwise. action_gap is the space between the buttons and body_gap the space above them — make it wider than the button gap so the question and the choice read as two parts. For one dialog only, call set_next_action_layout() before opening it. The row is built when a dialog first opens, so an autoloaded GoDialogs adds nothing at startup.","if await dialogs.confirm(\"Delete save\", \"This cannot be undone.\"): delete_save()",-1],[6,"goform-a-width-capped-form","GoForm — a width-capped form",1,"GoForm It guarantees its descendant labels wrap. Without that, one long sentence stretches into a single line whose minimum width exceeds the screen, and the sides are clipped — you cannot even tell what screen you are on. Turning wrapping on by hand per scene is forgotten every time.","",-1],[6,"goscroll-touch-scrolling","GoScroll — touch scrolling",1,"GoScroll · GoScroll.horizontal() Put one thing inside it. Headers and button rows belong outside — a long list must not push them off screen. use_panel_edge() moves the scrollbar into the card's existing padding while the content keeps its indent.","",-1],[7,"gonotice-snackbar","GoNotice — snackbar",1,"GoNotice GoSnackbar It never intercepts input. A notice is read, not pressed. It takes no focus, does not block game input, and the button beneath it still presses. When confirmation is needed use GoDialogs; when a choice is needed, GoPromptCard.","",-1],[7,"gopromptcard-a-question-that-does-not-block","GoPromptCard — a question that does not block",1,"GoPromptCard Floats at one side with no scrim. The game keeps running.","",-1],[7,"gocoachmark-guided-tour","GoCoachMark — guided tour",1,"GoCoachMark Points at real controls one at a time. Only the card takes input, so pressing the highlighted control itself advances the tour — \"press here\" becomes an action rather than a sentence. title and body may be translation keys or plain text. A step whose target has disappeared is skipped.","tour.start([ {\"target\": bag_button, \"title\": \"Bag\", \"body\": \"Everything you pick up lands here.\"}, {\"target\": map_button, \"title\": \"Map\", \"body\": \"Press to open the full map.\"}, ])",-1],[8,"the-small-things-decide-whether-it-looks-good","The small things decide whether it looks good",1,"Polish the big panels all you like — what catches the eye is always something small: a word split in two, a glow chopped off, a cramped slot. Four such things were pointed out on 2026-09-13 and fixed in the widgets and themes, not in the demo screen, so every screen gets the same result. What showed Cause Fix The coach mark's Done became Don/e A button with wrapping on subtracts its text width from its minimum — squeeze it and it breaks inside a word GoStyle.fit_words(): one word never wraps; several words wrap, but the longest word always fits — judged on the displayed text, not the translation key, and re-applied by the form when the language changes A full-width button's glow cut off vertically on the left A scroll container clips at its edge, no exceptions. Only the right survived, thanks to the rail gutter GoScroll borrows the parent's padding to push its edge 12dp out and gives it back inside — content stays put Time, icon and count stacked vertically in a slot Three rows inside 48dp Icon large in the centre, shortcut top-left, count as a bottom-right badge, remaining time as a badge over the icon — badge panels come from the skin's badge_box() A flat dropdown with no visible selection Item hover used the button panel; radio marks were the engine's faint default A dedicated hover panel (soft accent tint), the same radio artwork as checkboxes, item height sized for touch Dropdown — hover panel and radio mark Slots — corner badges and remaining time (sci-fi) Give icon-only buttons a description with GoStyle.icon_button(icon, action, -1, tooltip_key) — the tooltip for mouse users and the accessibility name for screen readers both come from that one value. gohud draws the tooltip itself: the engine's default splits the text one character per line when its width calculation goes wrong (measured at 1dp wide). The coach-mark card keeps off fixtures In landscape the card used to be sent to the very top or bottom edge — exactly where headers and HUD pieces live; in the demo it sat on the header's → ×. It now stays level with its target, steps around any GoHudAnchor that reserves space, and takes other things to avoid via keep_clear. It moves the shortest distance that clears the obstacle without covering the target, and stays put when the screen is too small to clear everything — overlapping beats vanishing. Its depth — so it reads as above the page — comes from skin dials (float_shadow_size, float_shadow_lift, float_shadow_alpha; chamfered skins use float_glow_size).","tour.keep_clear = [header_bar, toolbar] # fixtures that are not anchors",-1],[8,"screens-with-a-mouse-and-a-keyboard","Screens with a mouse and a keyboard",1,"A finger has no hover state. Build against mobile only and two desktop-only states go unchecked — and one of them was broken: gohud's focus ring was invisible on a primary button. The panel is the accent colour and so was the ring: 1.00:1, the same colour drawn over itself. Moving by keyboard, there was no way to tell where you were. Top to bottom: normal · hover · focus. Filled buttons get a ring that contrasts with their panel. Filled buttons (GoPrimaryButton, GoDangerSolidButton) use a ring that contrasts with their own panel — dark on a dark theme, white on a light one, a dark targeting bracket in sci-fi. The contrast checker measures the focus ring against the panel it sits on, so the rule survives a palette change (WCAG 2.4.11 asks for 3:1 on focus indicators).","",-1],[8,"hud-widgets","The HUD widgets",0,"","",-1],[8,"gohudanchor-nine-spots","GoHudAnchor — nine spots",1,"TOP_LEFT · TOP_RIGHT · BOTTOM_LEFT · BOTTOM_RIGHT Respects the safe area and edge margins. Give it a landscape_spot and it moves in landscape — controls that sit bottom-centre in portrait can go bottom-right instead. Why it exists. Written by hand per HUD piece, anchors and offsets drift: a health bar ends up under the camera cutout on a notched device, and a control button lands on the gesture bar in landscape. That arithmetic lives in one place. Keeping content out from under the HUD When a scrolling screen shares the display with a HUD, the content slides underneath it and the two sets of text overlap until neither can be read. It happened twice in this add-on: an input's placeholder squeezed out between the quick slots, and a settings toggle's knob landed on the health bar. Each rectangle is avoided in whichever direction costs the least area. A bar in the top-right is stepped around downwards on a portrait phone (13% of the height) and sideways in landscape (21% of the width) — avoiding it vertically in landscape would cost 27% of the screen. Ground already given up is subtracted before the next rectangle is measured. HUD pieces collide with each other too The nine spots divide the screen; they do not guarantee the pieces miss each other. A wide snackbar at top-centre landed squarely on the health bar at top-right, hiding the value — you could not read how much health was left. It steps aside vertically only — moving sideways as well would make a centred toast appear in a different place each time it shows. And it only avoids pieces that are not stepping aside themselves: if both yield, the two swap places forever.","form.avoid_hud = true # keep clear of every visible GoHudAnchor joystick_anchor.reserve_space = false # …except ones that only appear under a finger notice_anchor.avoid_peers = true # settles below the fixed HUD notice_anchor.reserve_space = false # and does not push the page while it is up",116],[8,"gobar-health-mana-experience","GoBar — health, mana, experience",1,"GoBar Changes ease over 0.18s — a health bar that jumps does not tell you how hard you were hit. reduce_motion makes it instant. Large numbers abbreviate to 12.3k so the bar's width does not jitter as digits come and go.","var hp := GoBar.new() hp.label_text = \"HP\" hp.ink = GoUi.color(GoTheme.DANGER_FILL) # the fill-only token hp.set_values(320, 500) # \"320 / 500\"",116],[8,"goslot-one-quick-slot","GoSlot — one quick slot",1,"GoSlot GoSlotGrid Icon, quantity, cooldown and shortcut on a single face. Hanging badges off a small circle makes each slot a different width and the row wobbles. Visible size and touch size differ. Packed slots have overlapping 48dp touch boxes; the overlap goes to whichever slot's centre is nearer — tell them about each other through touch_peers. keyboard_focus is off by default, so a row of eight slots does not sit between a keyboard user and every settings control in the Tab order. Turn it on when a keyboard or gamepad is the only input.","",116],[8,"gojoystick-virtual-stick","GoJoystick — virtual stick",1,"GoJoystick Mode Behaviour FIXED Always the same place — easy to find without looking FOLLOW Appears where the thumb lands RELATIVE Keeps following the thumb after appearing — comfortable for long movement The Vector2 from moved has length 0–1, so you can multiply it straight into a speed; it does not vary with screen size or DPI.","",116],[8,"goiconbutton-looks-small-presses-large","GoIconButton — looks small, presses large",1,"GoIconButton Only safe while its siblings ignore input. If the widened area covers the next button, that button stops responding. Side-by-side icon buttons need touch_peers.","",116],[9,"gosnackbar-the-message-that-places-itself","GoSnackbar — the message that places itself",1,"GoSnackbar Sits at the bottom (or the top), above the safe area and the keyboard, and leaves on its own. Without it you write the layer, the placement, the timer and the teardown on every screen that has to say \"saved\". Messages queue instead of overwriting each other, and repeats of the same line are merged — a server failing four times a second no longer stacks four minutes of alerts. A snackbar with no button lets input through, so the game underneath keeps running. It is not a place to ask something. It goes away by itself, so the player may never see it. Irreversible confirmations belong in GoDialogs. Buttons here must be optional — Undo, Details, Retry. GoNotice is the other half of the pair: it never takes input or focus, and the screen that owns it decides where it goes. It cannot hold a button; this can.","snack.show_text(\"Saved\", GoTheme.SUCCESS) # A chance to undo — 0 is the first button, -1 means it timed out if await snack.post({\"text\": \"Item dropped\", \"actions\": [\"Undo\"]}) == 0: restore_item()",-1],[9,"gospinner-a-wait-with-no-end-in-sight","GoSpinner — a wait with no end in sight",1,"GoSpinner.busy() · GoSpinner Games that talk to a server need this more than anything else on this page: a screen that sits still reads as a crash. One call turns the button you pressed into a spinner in place. The button keeps its size — the label goes transparent rather than away, so the row does not jump — and it is disabled while it spins. That second part is the point: a purchase must not fire twice while you await. With reduce_motion on it does not spin; three dots pulse instead. Progress you can measure is a GoBar. A spinner promises nothing about when it ends.","GoSpinner.busy(buy_button, true) var ok := await server.purchase(item) GoSpinner.busy(buy_button, false)",-1],[9,"gobadge-the-unread-dot-the-new-tag-the-99","GoBadge — the unread dot, the NEW tag, the 99+",1,"GoBadge It hangs on the host's top-right corner with anchors, so it follows a host whose size is decided later, and attaching twice returns the same badge. Use a number when the count changes what the player does, a dot when only \"there is something\" matters. Its text colour is chosen for contrast against whatever colour the skin painted the badge — never assumed white — and it carries an accessible name, because a coloured dot says nothing to a screen reader.","GoBadge.attach(mail_button, unread_count) # hides itself at zero GoBadge.attach(shop_button, 0, \"NEW\") GoBadge.attach(friend_button, 3, \"\", true) # a dot — \"something is there\"",-1],[10,"gofield-the-row-that-can-be-wrong","GoField — the row that can be wrong",1,"GoField · set_error() One line at the top of a five-field form saying \"check your input\" does not say which field. That single thing is what makes people abandon a sign-up. The hint hides while an error shows, so the row does not grow by a line and push everything below it, and the error text is joined into the control's accessible name — a red border alone says nothing to someone who cannot see red. GoStyle.field() is the static version: label, control, hint, no error state. Use the factory when nothing can go wrong and the node for anything a server can reject.","var name_field := GoField.make(\"Character name\", GoStyle.line_edit(\"2-12\"), \"Cannot be changed later\") name_field.set_error(\"That name is taken\") # the server said no name_field.clear_error()",-1],[10,"goinputgroup-an-input-welded-to-its-button","GoInputGroup — an input welded to its button",1,"GoInputGroup What it solves is corners. Two rounded shapes meeting in the middle look pinched, and the default gap makes them read as two objects. Outer corners stay round, touching ones go square — in every button state, or the group splits the moment it is pressed. Chamfered skins have no corner fields at all, so there it leaves them alone and the square faces meet cleanly.","GoInputGroup.make(GoStyle.line_edit(\"Message\"), {\"suffix\": GoStyle.icon_button(&\"send\", send)}) GoInputGroup.make(GoStyle.line_edit(\"Name\"), {\"prefix_icon\": &\"search\"})",-1],[10,"gocombobox-a-picker-that-searches","GoCombobox — a picker that searches",1,"GoCombobox Under ten entries GoStyle.select() is better: one less tap and the whole list is visible. Past thirty, scanning is work. The search matches inside names, not just their start. Prefix matching finds almost nothing in Korean or Japanese lists, where the word that tells two items apart is rarely the first one.","var picker := GoCombobox.make(server_names, 0, \"Choose a server\") picker.picked.connect(func(i: int) -> void: connect_to(servers[i]))",-1],[10,"gocodeinput-coupon-and-gift-codes","GoCodeInput — coupon and gift codes",1,"GoCodeInput A code is pasted from a message far more often than it is typed. Twelve real fields would break pasting at the first cell and lose characters to an IME, so one hidden field takes the text and the cells are drawn. ABCD-EFGH-IJKL loses its dashes on the way in.","var coupon := GoCodeInput.make(12, 4) coupon.completed.connect(func(code: String) -> void: server.redeem(code)) coupon.set_error(\"Already used\")",-1],[10,"gotable-sortable-headers-selectable-rows","GoTable — sortable headers, selectable rows",1,"GoTable numeric: true, or the ranking inverts. Compared as text, \"9124\" beats \"91240\" — and scores, gold and damage all have mixed digit counts. row_selected gives the index in your original array, not the sorted position. The sort direction is shown with a glyph, not only a colour, and whole rows are pressable so nobody has to hit one cell. GoStyle.table() remains the read-only grid.","var board := GoTable.make( [{\"text\": \"Rank\", \"width\": 56}, {\"text\": \"Name\"}, {\"text\": \"Score\", \"numeric\": true}], rows) board.row_selected.connect(func(i: int) -> void: open_profile(rows[i]))",-1],[10,"gopagination-pages-or-a-more-row","GoPagination — pages, or a More row",1,"GoPagination Numbers are a mouse UI; on a phone the More row reads better. The current page stays centred in the window, so pressing next does not reshuffle every number. A total of 0 means \"unknown\" and only the arrows are drawn — it does not invent a page count it was not given.","var pager := GoPagination.make(1, 12, func(page: int) -> void: load_mail(page)) var more := GoPagination.more(load_next) # the mobile-friendly variant",-1],[11,"gorewardcalendar-daily-attendance","GoRewardCalendar — daily attendance",1,"GoRewardCalendar A date picker is almost never useful in a game. A calendar shape is — for attendance rewards, where what matters is which day you are on, not which date it is. Only today's cell can be pressed — a button that does nothing when pressed reads as broken. Claimed, today and future differ by three things at once: a tick glyph, an accent border and dimming.","var attendance := GoRewardCalendar.make(days, claimed_until) attendance.claimed.connect(func(day: int) -> void: server.claim_day(day))",-1],[11,"goradar-and-godonut-stats-at-a-glance","GoRadar and GoDonut — stats at a glance",1,"GoRadar GoDonut Radar values are 0–1 because what counts as full is a game decision — raw 120 STR beside 45 INT would draw a lie. Donut values are raw and it divides for you; past five slices it collapses the rest, since a sixth slice is a thread nobody can read. The comparison line is dashed, not just another colour, and the legend prints the percentage in words.","var stats := GoRadar.make({\"STR\": 0.85, \"AGI\": 0.5, \"INT\": 0.3, \"VIT\": 0.7, \"LUK\": 0.45}) stats.set_compare(with_new_sword) # a dashed overlay var share := GoDonut.make([{\"label\": \"Physical\", \"value\": 620}, {\"label\": \"Magic\", \"value\": 340}]) card.add_child(share.legend())",-1],[11,"gocarousel-banners-and-character-select","GoCarousel — banners and character select",1,"GoCarousel It does not advance on its own unless you ask, and five seconds is the floor: a banner that changes every three takes the text away before it is read. Touching it resets the timer, and with reduce_motion on it never advances by itself. The dots are pressable at the touch minimum even though the drawn dot is small.","banners.set_pages([promo, event, pack]) banners.autoplay_seconds = 5.0 # off by default",-1],[11,"gokbd-key-hints-that-do-not-lie","GoKbd — key hints that do not lie",1,"GoKbd A hard-coded \"Press F\" keeps saying F after the player rebinds — the most common lie in a PC UI. for_action() reads InputMap; if the action is bound to a pad instead, it returns empty and the widget hides, because \"None\" would be its own lie. On Android and iOS it hides itself.","hint.add_child(GoKbd.for_action(&\"interact\")) # reads the real binding",-1],[12,"godrawer-the-side-panel","GoDrawer — the side panel",1,"Side.LEFT Side.RIGHT GoSheet comes from the bottom, which is right for a phone held upright. On a tablet or a desktop the same sheet covers the game; a drawer comes from the side instead. The panel reaches the screen edge but the content stays inside the safe area, or a rounded corner clips the first row. LEFT means screen-left even in Arabic; turn on follow_text_direction when \"the start side\" is the point, and it flips in RTL.","bag.side = GoDrawer.Side.RIGHT bag.open(\"Bag\")",-1],[12,"gopopover-the-anchored-card","GoPopover — the anchored card",1,"GoPopover This is GoSurface's anchored placement with the layer, the surface, the anchor and the teardown already wired — the ten lines every game writes over and over. One is open at a time, because stacked cards bury the screen and nobody can tell which card belongs to which slot. The scrim is transparent: a card you opened to compare gear must not darken the gear. It is not a hover tooltip. Touch has no hover, so anything only a mouse could reveal is invisible to half your players.","GoPopover.open(slot, item_card(item))",-1],[12,"gocontextmenu-long-press-and-right-click","GoContextMenu — long-press and right-click",1,"GoContextMenu PopupMenu is already in the engine. What is not is the gesture: half a second to open, cancelled the moment the finger moves, so scrolling a list never pops a menu. Pass a Callable instead of an array when the entries depend on who you pressed. A long press needs a second way in. Nobody discovers a hidden gesture — pair it with a visible ⋯ button (open_at()), an icon, or a first-run coach mark.","GoContextMenu.attach(item_slot, [ {\"text\": \"Use\", \"action\": use}, {\"separator\": true}, {\"text\": \"Drop\", \"action\": drop, \"danger\": true}, ])",-1],[12,"goconsole-the-developer-console","GoConsole — the developer console",1,"GoConsole Cheat and debug commands, with a palette that filters as you type so nobody has to memorise them, and a history on the arrow keys. It sits above everything, so you can debug over a dialog. It refuses to open in a release build. debug_only is on by default; cheat commands in a player's hands end a game's economy on the first day.","console.register(\"give\", \"Grant an item: give <id> <count>\", give) console.toggle()",-1],[13,"list-rows-with-a-description","List rows with a description",1,"GoStyle.list_button() A row with a second line gets equal top and bottom padding, roomier than a single-line row, and the title/description pair stays vertically centred beside the icon — also when a container stretches the row taller, and after the description wraps onto several lines. The whole row remains one tap target. Two-line rows, slots and bars in the medieval example — the same factory calls under medieval_light.","GoStyle.list_button(GoIconSet.SWORD, \"Oathkeeper\", _inspect, Color.TRANSPARENT, \"Longsword / Attack 42\", false)",-1],[13,"flowing-rows","Flowing rows",1,"row() · wrap_row() Put controls into wrap_row at their natural width. With wrapping left on, a button's minimum width drops to almost nothing and the row sizes its cell by it — the label collapses to one character per line. The factory prevents this for you.","",-1],[13,"never-leave-an-empty-list-empty","Never leave an empty list empty",1,"skeleton() · empty_state() People read a blank screen as broken.","page.add_child(GoStyle.empty_state(GoIconSet.BOX, \"Nothing here yet\"))",-1],[13,"hooks","Subclass hooks",0,"Every place a child widget is constructed goes through an overridable method, so a project that subclasses gohud types can get its own subclasses inside the widgets without copying code. Hook Widget Default _make_scroll() GoCoachMark, GoSurface GoScroll.new() _make_close_button() GoPromptCard, GoSurface GoIconButton.new() _make_surface() GoSheet, GoDialogs GoSurface.new() _should_pause() GoCoachMark Hides the card while a modal is open","",-1],[15,"pick","Picking one",0,"That one line swaps theme, skin and icons. From the editor, use Project Settings → Gohud → Theme → Preset; from a settings resource, GoConfig.preset.","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.SCIFI_DARK)",-1],[15,"keeping-one-field-your-own","Keeping one field your own",1,"Setting theme, skin or icons explicitly wins over the preset.","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.SCIFI_DARK) GoUi.config.icons = my_icons # your icons, the preset's everything else",143],[15,"the-six-built-in-presets","The fourteen built-in presets",1,"Preset Panels Skin · icons default_dark · default_light Rounded StyleBoxFlat panels on a graded shadow scale; primary buttons lift and sink when pressed GoSkin · 84 default icons scifi_dark · scifi_light Chamfered GoStyleBoxCut panels with a neon edge and glow; GoStyleBoxBracket focus marks GoSkinSciFi — hexagonal joystick · default icons medieval_dark · medieval_light Forged GoStyleBoxMedieval frames — iron and leather, or parchment — with rivets and corner ornaments on menus GoSkinMedieval · 16 engraved icons over the defaults material_light · material_dark New Material 3 Expressive for app screens — pill buttons with a 40dp plate in the 48dp touch target, 28dp dialogs, filled cards, outlined fields, the Expressive slider; the app components (navigation bar, app bar, FAB, search bar, chips, progress, date picker) follow the M3 component tokens GoSkinMaterial · default icons kids_light · kids_dark New For children — the toy box: chunky outlines and a solid lip under every key, which sinks when pressed; sunken text fields, bubble tabs, jelly bars; each kind of control in its own crayon colour, candy quick slots, sticker badges, a rainbow joystick and crayon charts. Sizes and the project's font stay as they are. GoSkinKids · default icons arcade_light · arcade_dark New An arcade cabinet drawn by GoStyleBoxArcade: every key painted with a top-to-bottom gradient, a white gloss and a lip that sinks when pressed, in a navy ink outline, its label white with an ink outline — green primary, blue keys, red danger, lavender small keys. Thick boards with a coloured frame round a pale well; a gold title banner and a round red close key on windows. GoSkinArcade · default icons comic_light · comic_dark New Comic-book panels drawn by GoStyleBoxComic: a bold ink outline and a hard shadow on every face, which goes when the face is pressed; inked toggles, check boxes and slider handles, a yellow title caption on windows. The outline width, the shadow size and whether shadows show at all are GoConfig settings. GoSkinComic · default icons","",143],[15,"all-looks","All fourteen, side by side",0,"The same gallery screen with only the preset name changed — not a line of widget code differs. Each one is a phone held upright, 390×844. default_dark default_light scifi_dark scifi_light medieval_dark medieval_light material_light material_dark kids_light kids_dark comic_light comic_dark arcade_light arcade_dark","",-1],[15,"medieval","Medieval: iron, leather and parchment",0,"medieval_dark pairs dark iron and leather with antique gold. medieval_light uses parchment and ink. Both use GoSkinMedieval, the existing widgets, and 16 original icons with engraving details; navigation icons fall back to the original set. Choose the preset before creating your UI. Explicit GoConfig.theme, skin or icons overrides still take precedence. Open res://addons/gohud/examples/medieval/medieval.tscn and press F6 for a working character sheet, satchel and quest journal. Its buttons switch variants and open item details. Iron and leather Parchment and ink Menu frames have a rivet and small corner ornament; the always-visible HUD keeps a quiet edge. HP, mana and stamina use red, blue and olive fills. Cinzel is scoped to titles and subtitles; body text keeps the host/default font. The bundled font includes its license at assets/fonts/cinzel/OFL.txt. The engraved set redraws bag, book, box, coin, crown, flag, heart, key, map, potion, shield, star, sword and user, and adds scroll and seal. Every other name falls back to the default set, so close and settings keep their default drawings in every preset. Cinzel covers Latin script; give localized headings a font of their own through shape.fonts. What the suite checks for both variants. The medieval skin is selected; menu and HUD panels are forged frames, with the ornament on menus only; titles use Cinzel while body text keeps the inherited font; engraved icons import as DPITexture; a real quick slot uses the skin; changing a copied skin's dials reaches the slot without touching the preset; and switching back restores the default and sci-fi geometry.","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MEDIEVAL_DARK) # Or: GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MEDIEVAL_LIGHT)",-1],[15,"make-a-kingdom-of-your-own","Make a kingdom of your own",1,"JSON themes can inherit other JSON themes. Omitted values keep their parent's settings; circular inheritance is rejected. The generated preset keeps its parent's icon set. Setting Effect shape.material 0: iron · 1: leather · 2: parchment. Controls the surface marks. shape.grain_alpha Texture opacity. Use 0 for a clean surface. shape.ornament_scale · shape.bevel_strength Menu corner ornament size and bevel highlight intensity. shape.fonts Map title, subtitle, caption, body and button roles to addon-local res:// font files. Omitted roles keep their inherited font. skin.dials Quick-slot radius, rivet visibility, grain and highlight. The full table below lists each dial.","python3 addons/gohud/tools/new_theme.py kingdom --from medieval_dark # Edit themes/palettes/kingdom.json, then: python3 addons/gohud/tools/make_theme.py kingdom godot --headless --path . --import # In GDScript, before creating the widgets: GoUi.use_preset(&\"kingdom\")",147],[15,"material","Material 3: a look for app screens New",0,"material_light and material_dark bring Material 3 Expressive to gohud — the shapes, sizes and type of the M3 components, with every number read from the official M3 token set (material-web, tokens/versions/latest). Reach for them where a screen should feel like an app rather than a game menu: shops, inboxes, account and settings pages, leaderboards, a companion app. material_light material_dark GoDialogs · material_light GoDialogs · material_dark","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MATERIAL_LIGHT) # Or: GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MATERIAL_DARK)",-1],[15,"what-changes","What changes",1,"Part In Material 3 Buttons Pills (the full corner). The plate is 40dp tall, centred in the 48dp touch target, so the press area does not shrink; a compact button's plate is 32dp. Labels use Roboto at weight 500. Dialogs and sheets 28dp corners (extra-large), 24dp padding and a 24sp headline — GoDialogs, GoSurface, GoSheet and every popup built on them. Cards Filled cards with 12dp corners and 16dp padding. Fields and sliders Outlined text fields; the Expressive slider with its tall handle. Chips and segments 8dp corners (small). App components GoNavBar, GoAppBar, GoFab, GoSearchBar, the chips, GoProgress and GoDatePicker follow the M3 component tokens. Type The bundled Roboto for titles, subtitles, captions and buttons. Body text keeps your project's font, so Korean, Japanese, Chinese or Arabic still draw. Opacity Every panel is opaque — M3 surfaces are solid. (Default, sci-fi and medieval panels are 80% opaque, so the game shows through.) Skin GoSkinMaterial: the drawer is the M3 modal side sheet, the console face is the M3 floating toolbar, banners sit on surface_container_low. Where the spec gives way to legibility. M3 fades a disabled label to 38%; gohud keeps it at 4.5:1 so it can still be read. Snackbars keep a light plate, because their text colour is a token the widget picks — an inverse plate would put dark text on dark. tools/check_contrast.py measures both looks like every other. Roboto is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (assets/fonts/roboto/OFL.txt) and is used by the Material presets only.","",149],[15,"kids","Kids: the toy box New",0,"kids_light (cream and peach with a grape primary) and kids_dark (blueberry ground, sunny-yellow primary, mint pills) are a look made for children's games and learning apps — chunky, bright and squishy, the kind of thing a small finger wants to press. kids_light kids_dark GoDialogs · kids_light GoDialogs · kids_dark","GoUi.use_preset(&\"kids_light\") # Or: GoUi.use_preset(&\"kids_dark\")",-1],[15,"what-changes-2","What changes",1,"Part In the kids looks Every face A jelly candy, drawn by GoStyleBoxJelly: a chunky outline, a solid lip under everything you press, a body lighter on top and deeper below, and a white shine at the top left. Keys, list rows, folding titles, fields, bars, sliders and panels all wear it. Pressing The lip goes and the face sinks into its place, then a jelly squish — wide and flat for a moment, then an elastic spring back. It runs on every button gohud makes; reduce_motion turns it off. Fields, tabs, bars A text field is the same jelly turned in — a sunken well. Tabs are bubbles, bars have a jelly shine. Colour Each kind of control in its own crayon colour, chosen by the same generator as every look, so every contrast gate still holds. Windows A sunny ribbon (mint at night) behind a window's title — the title shrinks, down to 15, to stay on one line — and a round candy close button in the danger crayon with a white cross. Skin parts GoSkinKids: quick slots are candy blocks that sink while cooling down, badges are stickers, chips and the navigation pill are small jellies, avatars are round candies, the joystick is a rainbow, charts use crayons, alerts and notices are sticker notes with a solid rim. Opacity Panels, cards, notices and popups are opaque. No size changes. The outline and the lip are drawn inside each control's rectangle and every face keeps the padding the theme gave it, so a screen laid out in another look keeps its layout, and a host that pins its own sizes measures the same parts. Your project's font is kept too, so non-Latin scripts still draw. The parts a skin draws — the kids row is second","",151],[15,"make-a-toy-box-of-your-own","Make a toy box of your own",1,"","python3 addons/gohud/tools/new_theme.py candy --from kids_light # Edit themes/palettes/candy.json, then: python3 addons/gohud/tools/make_theme.py candy GoUi.use_preset(&\"candy\")",151],[15,"comic","Comic: bold ink New",0,"comic_light (white panels on a paper-cream page, a cobalt primary) and comic_dark (slate panels on a night page, cream outlines, a yellow primary) draw every face like a comic-book panel — a bold ink outline with a hard shadow behind it. comic_light comic_dark GoDialogs · comic_light GoDialogs · comic_dark","GoUi.use_preset(&\"comic_light\") # Or: GoUi.use_preset(&\"comic_dark\")",-1],[15,"what-changes-3","What changes",1,"Part In the comic looks Every face Drawn by GoStyleBoxComic: the surface colour inside a bold outline in the ink colour, and a hard shadow down and to the right. Keys, list rows, fields, tabs, bars, sliders, panels and popups all wear it. Pressing The shadow goes and the face sinks into its place. Controls Toggles, check boxes, radio buttons and slider handles are inked too, each with its own small shadow. Windows A yellow caption behind a window's title and an inked round close button. Skin parts GoSkinComic: quick slots, chips, badges, avatars, notices, the navigation bar, the FAB and the date cells are inked; the joystick knob casts a shadow; charts use bold primaries. Opacity Panels, cards, notices and popups are opaque; HUD cards are 92% opaque.","",154],[15,"ink-and-shadow-settings","Ink and shadow settings",1,"Three GoConfig settings change every comic face at once. Nothing is rebuilt — the screen redraws as you set them. One widget can go its own way, whatever the setting says: No size changes. The outline and the shadow are drawn inside each control's rectangle and every face keeps the padding the theme gave it, so a screen laid out in another look keeps its layout. Your project's font is kept too. The parts the comic skin draws","GoUi.config.comic_border_width = 2.0 # the outline (dp) — 3 by default GoUi.config.comic_shadow_size = 6.0 # the shadow (dp) — 4 by default GoUi.config.comic_shadow = false # no shadows anywhere GoStyle.comic_shadow(skip_button, false) # this button sits flat GoStyle.comic_shadow(card, true, true) # this card and everything in it keep their shadow GoStyle.comic_border(title, 5.0) # a thicker outline on this one",154],[15,"make-a-comic-of-your-own","Make a comic of your own",1,"","python3 addons/gohud/tools/new_theme.py inked --from comic_light # Edit themes/palettes/inked.json, then: python3 addons/gohud/tools/make_theme.py inked GoUi.use_preset(&\"inked\")",154],[15,"arcade","Arcade: painted keys and thick boards New",0,"arcade_light (white boards on a sky-blue page) and arcade_dark (navy boards on a night page) dress every screen like an arcade cabinet: every key is painted — a gradient from a light top to a deeper bottom, a white gloss stroke and a lip that sinks when pressed, inside a navy ink outline — and every board is thick, a coloured frame round a pale well. arcade_light arcade_dark GoDialogs · arcade_light GoDialogs · arcade_dark","GoUi.use_preset(&\"arcade_light\") # Or: GoUi.use_preset(&\"arcade_dark\")",-1],[15,"what-changes-4","What changes",1,"Part In the arcade looks Keys Drawn by GoStyleBoxArcade: a gradient body, a white gloss round the top-left corner, a deeper lip and a navy ink outline. The primary key is green, normal keys and the chosen tab blue, danger keys coral and red, small keys and the other tabs lavender. Labels White with an ink outline on every painted key. Every paint is moved until that label reads at every height of its gradient — 4.6:1 or more, outline counted as part of the letter, as WCAG does. Pressing The lip goes, the key sinks into its place and pops back. Boards Panels, cards, HUD cards and popups are thick: a coloured frame (6dp round a window, 4 round a card or a HUD card, 3 round a menu or a notice) with its own gloss and lip, round a pale well with an ink line. Their padding grows a little to hold it, so text never touches the frame. Fields and bars Text fields and bar grooves are sunken wells; a bar's fill is a glossy painted tube in the bright fill of its colour. Windows A gold banner with a white, ink-outlined title, and a round red close key with a white cross. Skin parts GoSkinArcade: quick slots and chips are key caps, a cooling slot lights a gold rim, badges are light plates, alerts are framed in their colour, the chosen card lights a gold rim, the FAB is a gold key and the joystick a glossy pad with four arrows. Opacity Panels, cards, notices and popups are opaque; HUD cards are 94% opaque.","",158],[15,"paint-one-key-its-own-colour","Paint one key its own colour",1,"The theme paints keys by kind. A menu whose keys each want their own colour paints them one by one — the hover face comes a little lighter, the pressed one a little deeper, and the disabled face stays dim: The label always reads. A paint the white label would not read on is moved lighter or deeper until it does, so the colour you pass is a starting point. Under the other looks arcade_paint() does nothing. Keys keep their size. The lip and the gloss are drawn inside each key's rectangle, so a screen laid out in another look keeps its layout. Boards pad their content a little more (a card and a HUD card 12dp, 15 at the bottom) so the text never touches the frame. Your project's font is kept too. The parts the arcade skin draws","menu.add_child(GoStyle.arcade_paint(GoStyle.button(\"Resume\", _resume, GoStyle.Tone.PRIMARY), Color(\"#4ACB3E\"))) menu.add_child(GoStyle.arcade_paint(GoStyle.button(\"Shop\", _shop), Color(\"#FF8A1E\"))) GoStyle.arcade_paint(stage_card, Color(\"#E3343D\"), true) # a board's frame, and every key inside it",158],[15,"make-an-arcade-of-your-own","Make an arcade of your own",1,"","python3 addons/gohud/tools/new_theme.py cabinet --from arcade_light # Edit themes/palettes/cabinet.json — the *_vivid colours are the paints — then: python3 addons/gohud/tools/make_theme.py cabinet GoUi.use_preset(&\"cabinet\")",158],[16,"colours","Colours",1,"Name Used for background The screen floor surface · surface_soft · surface_high Three panel layers — panel, card, raised cell border Card and button borders text · secondary · muted Three text levels — body, supporting, dimmed accent · on_accent The accent and the text placed on it success · warning · danger · info Status text colours *_fill The same statuses as a fill — bars and other large areas scrim · shadow · track The veil behind popups, shadows, the bar's trough Why *_fill exists. The same meaning, opposite requirements. warning used as text must be dark enough to read on a light background; used as an experience bar's fill it must be bright enough to notice. One token cannot be both — the light theme's bar went brown. A theme without the _fill variant falls back to the base name automatically, so themes that predate these tokens keep working.","",-1],[16,"measurements-dp","Measurements (dp)",1,"touch button_height gap_tiny gap_small gap gap_large padding padding_compact compact_padding_x compact_padding_y radius_small radius radius_large screen_margin scroll_deadzone scroll_edge scrollbar_width list_glyph icon_size notice_duration_ms","",-1],[16,"panel-opacity","Panel opacity (%)",1,"panel_alpha card_alpha hud_alpha notice_alpha popup_alpha — how solid a container's face is. 80 by default, so the game stays visible behind a dialog; popup_alpha is 100. A theme without these tokens falls back to 100 and draws exactly as it did before. Read the resolved value as a ratio with GoUi.surface_alpha(variant); the section Opacity — the game behind the panel has the rules.","",-1],[16,"text-roles","Text roles",1,"micro · compact · caption · body · button · subtitle · title — a role names a size, not a purpose. \"The largest text\", not \"the heading\". That way the scale holds even when a screen uses it for something else.","",-1],[16,"type-variations","Type variations",1,"GoPanel GoCard GoButton GoPrimaryButton GoDangerButton GoDangerSolidButton GoPrimaryGlowButton GoDangerSolidGlowButton GoBareButton GoCompactButton GoIconButton GoListButton GoTitleLabel GoSubtitleLabel GoCaptionLabel GoCompactLabel GoMicroLabel","",-1],[17,"five-layers-most-specific-first","Five layers, most specific first",1,"Order Where Unit Reach ① the argument at that call — surface.alpha, GoStyle.card(…, alpha) ratio 0.0–1.0 one window ② GoConfig.container_alpha_overrides[kind] ratio 0.0–1.0 one kind of panel, project-wide ③ GoConfig.metric_overrides[<kind>_alpha] percent projects that keep every measurement in one place ④ GoConfig.container_alpha ratio 0.0–1.0 every panel at once ⑤ the theme's GoHud/constants/<kind>_alpha percent what the look decides — the source of truth With none of them set the value is 100, so nothing about an older theme changes. Opacity is a ratio everywhere — except in the theme. Every alpha field and argument takes 0.0–1.0, the same units as Color.a and modulate.a, and a negative value means \"not set\". The one exception is the theme's constants, because a Theme constant cannot hold a float: those and the channel that overrides them (metric_overrides, which shares the theme's names and integer type) are written as 80. Nothing else is.","# One window only — a confirm dialog that must not hide the fight behind it surface.alpha = 0.6 sheet.alpha = 0.7 dialogs.alpha = 0.9 # @export fields are ratios too drawer.alpha = 0.7 GoPopover.open(slot, body, {\"alpha\": 0.9}) var glass := GoStyle.card(Color.TRANSPARENT, -1.0, -1.0, -1.0, 0.5) # Per kind — keep the HUD nearly solid, because its text sits straight over the world GoUi.config.container_alpha_overrides = { GoTheme.BOX_PANEL: 0.7, # dialogs and sheets can breathe GoTheme.BOX_HUD: 0.95, } GoUi.refresh() # redraws widgets that are already open # The whole project — a busy world wants its panels back to solid GoUi.config.container_alpha = 1.0 GoUi.refresh() GoUi.surface_alpha(GoTheme.BOX_PANEL) # the resolved ratio, e.g. 0.8",-1],[17,"what-follows-the-value-and-what-does-not","What follows the value, and what does not",1,"Follows it — containers Ignores it — things you press, and markers GoSurface (the one shell behind dialogs, sheets and dropdowns) · GoSheet · GoDialogs · GoDrawer · GoPopover · GoNotice · GoSnackbar · GoPromptCard · GoCoachMark · GoConsole every button · GoSlot (quick slots) · GoBadge · segmented controls · choice cells · chips · discs and avatars GoStyle.card() · hud_panel() · overlay_panel() · alert() · plate() · edge_card_panel() · style_notice_panel() · floating() · box() · surface() all text and icons A button whose state is washed out no longer says what it is, and a badge exists to make two characters legible — neither is a container, so neither follows the value. Popup menus stay solid (popup_alpha 100). The engine may host a PopupMenu in its own Window, and there the OS does not composite it with the game: translucency comes out black rather than see-through. Lower it only in projects that embed their subwindows (gui_embed_subwindows).","",-1],[17,"three-details-that-come-from-real-screens","Three details that come from real screens",1,"The value multiplies, it does not replace. The default HUD face is already 0.92 alpha, so hud_alpha 80 lands at 0.736 — a theme that deliberately made a face translucent keeps that decision. The flip side: apply it twice and the panel fades twice, which is why the alpha is multiplied in exactly one place (GoSkin.surface_box()) and every other face function forwards the argument instead of fading its own result. A colour you passed is a colour you get. GoStyle.plate(…, fill) keeps an explicit fill exactly as given: Color(ink, 0.14) already states its alpha, and multiplying panel opacity into it would cut the caller's intent twice. GoStyle.floating(…, opaque = true) ignores the value for the same kind of reason — filling the face solid is that flag's whole purpose. Panels gohud did not build get the same rule. GoStyle.fade_panel(node) — after the node is in the tree, so it reads the theme it inherits. It is idempotent: the original face is recorded and every call recomputes from that, so repeated redraws never stack. After swapping themes, GoStyle.forget_face(node) drops that memory so the next call picks up the new face.","",-1],[17,"custom-faces-fade-too-and-that-is-the-part-that","Custom faces fade too — and that is the part that silently breaks",1,"The cut-corner panel (GoStyleBoxCut) and the forged frame (GoStyleBoxMedieval) are not StyleBoxFlat; they draw themselves. Put the opacity only in the flat branch and these themes quietly ignore it while every value-based test still passes. Both fade their background and keep glow, rivets, corner engraving and bevels at full strength — and the medieval face's grain and bevel were always proportional to its background alpha, so they thin out along with the panel. Which is the wider point: bg_color.a == 0.8 is a number. The world shows through and the text is still legible is the requirement. gohud checks the first in its headless suite and the second by drawing panels over diagonal stripes on a virtual monitor (tests/gohud_alpha_shot.gd) — on the flat, the cut and the forged face, in both the dark and the light theme.","",-1],[18,"shapes-styleboxflat-cannot-make","Shapes StyleBoxFlat cannot make",1,"Class What it draws GoStyleBoxCut Diagonally cut corners, one thickened accent edge, an outer glow GoStyleBoxBracket Corner marks only, leaving the content unenclosed GoStyleBoxMedieval A forged frame — rivets, corner engraving, a bevel highlight and iron, leather or parchment grain All three serialise into a Theme resource like any other StyleBox — which is what lets a theme change shape. Give padding through content_margin_*. Subclassing StyleBox in GDScript means _get_style_margin() is never called (measured on Godot 4.7). Fill the built-in fields or content will sit against the border.","",-1],[19,"what-you-can-change-on-one-page","What you can change — on one page",1,"Where What How from the parent theme dark · light · scifi_dark · medieval_dark · … or another JSON theme. Omitted keys inherit its values; an inheritance cycle fails palette background · three surfaces · border · three text tones · accent · four status colours · scrim · shadow · bar track \"#RRGGBB\", alpha as \"#RRGGBB@0.35\" fill-only vivid colours *_vivid keep bars saturated even when the text colour has to darken — leave one out and the builder says so readability not tuned by hand. Text, borders, the accent and the label on it are pushed by the builder until they clear the thresholds — change only the accent and the checks still pass shape kind flat (rounded) · cut (chamfered corners) · medieval (forged frames) sizes radius · radius_small · radius_large · gap · gap_small · gap_large · padding · button_height · button_padding[4] — the tokens follow, so panels and widget maths never disagree cut only cut_ratio · cut_max · corners (diagonal|all) · glow · edge medieval only material (0 iron · 1 leather · 2 parchment) · grain_alpha · ornament_scale · bevel_strength · fonts — title, subtitle, caption, body, button mapped to addon-local res:// font files skin base — the family for the places code draws itself (joystick, slots, badges, coach-mark ring, chips, dividers) default · scifi · medieval dials — the numbers of those places: slot border width and tint, badge padding, chip and alert opacity, joystick ring width and opacity, sci-fi chamfer sizes, glow and bracket Every parent value is spelled out in the JSON. The builder writes them into themes/skins/gohud_skin_<id>.tres — no skin code is touched. Only to change the drawings themselves do you run --new-skin, which scaffolds a GoSkin subclass icons the icon set a res:// path to a GoIconSet resource — kept from a JSON parent when omitted dark · title how the picker shows it boolean · string","",-1],[19,"every-dial","Every dial",1,"The table below is filled by tools/make_site.py straight from the skin scripts' @export lines — add a dial or change a default and the table follows. Use these names under skin.dials in the JSON. A dial whose default reads 14 is an integer, one that reads 10.0 a float — write either form in the JSON and the builder casts to the script's type. Default skin GoSkin — 17 Dial Default What it sets chip_fill_alpha 0.16 Fill opacity of a chip's panel. chip_edge_alpha 0.45 Edge opacity of a chip's panel. alert_tint 0.1 How far an alert box's panel is tinted toward its status colour. slot_tint_lit 0.24 Accent tint of a quick-slot panel while its cooldown runs. slot_tint_idle 0.08 Accent tint of a quick-slot panel at rest. slot_border_lit 2 Quick-slot border width (dp) while its cooldown runs. slot_border_idle 1 Quick-slot border width (dp) at rest. badge_pad_x 5 Horizontal inner padding (dp) of a badge (quantity, time left). badge_pad_y 1 Vertical inner padding (dp) of a badge. badge_edge_alpha 0.6 Edge opacity of a badge's panel. float_shadow_alpha 0.45 Shadow opacity of floating cards (coach mark, prompt card). float_shadow_size 14 Shadow blur (dp) of floating cards. float_shadow_lift 4 Downward offset (dp) of a floating card's shadow. float_glow_size 10.0 Glow distance (dp) of a floating panel that glows instead of casting a shadow, like the sci-fi chamfered panel. joystick_base_alpha 0.42 Opacity of the joystick's base disc. joystick_ring_alpha 0.45 Opacity of the joystick's ring. joystick_ring_width 2.0 Width (dp) of the joystick's ring. Sci-fi skin GoSkinSciFi — 10 Dial Default What it sets cut_chip 7.0 Chamfer size (dp) of a chip's panel. cut_skeleton 5.0 Chamfer size (dp) of a skeleton panel. cut_alert 8.0 Chamfer size (dp) of an alert box. cut_segment 8.0 Chamfer size (dp) of a segmented control. cut_slot 6.0 Chamfer size (dp) of a quick-slot panel. cut_disc_ratio 0.24 Chamfer of avatars and discs = diameter × this ratio. slot_glow_alpha 0.45 Glow opacity of a slot whose cooldown is running. slot_glow_size 6.0 Glow distance (dp) of a slot whose cooldown is running. bracket_arm 12.0 Arm length (dp) of the coach mark's targeting bracket. bracket_thickness 2.0 Line thickness (dp) of the coach mark's targeting bracket. Medieval skin GoSkinMedieval — 5 Dial Default What it sets slot_radius 4.0 Corner radius (dp) of the medieval quick-slot frame. leather_grain_alpha 0.035 Opacity of the subtle leather marks inside quick slots. ornament_scale 1.0 Scale of the metal decorations at quick-slot corners. Menu frames use shape.ornament_scale. bevel_strength 0.18 Strength of the metal highlight along quick-slot edges. slot_rivets 1 Show small metal rivets on quick slots: 0 hides them, 1 shows them. Material skin GoSkinMaterial — 2 Dial Default What it sets segment_gap 2.0 Space (dp) between the cells of a Material connected button group. segment_inner_radius 8 Corner radius (dp) where two cells of a Material connected button group meet. Kids skin GoSkinKids — 3 Dial Default What it sets toy_edge 2 Outline width (dp) of a kids toy part — chips, slots, the FAB, alerts. toy_lip 4 The solid lip (dp) under a kids toy part you press; it shrinks when the part is pressed. crayon_tint 0.28 How much crayon colour fills a kids slot or chip face (0–1); the rest is the surface colour. Comic skin GoSkinComic — 1 Dial Default What it sets comic_tint 0.22 How much of its own colour fills a comic chip, quick slot or chosen pill (0–1); the rest is the surface colour. Arcade skin GoSkinArcade — 5 Dial Default What it sets arcade_edge 3 Ink outline width (dp) of a part the arcade skin paints — slots, chips, badges, the title banner, the FAB. arcade_lip 4 The lip (dp) under an arcade part you press — keys, chips, slots, the FAB; it goes when the part is pressed. arcade_gloss 0.85 Strength of the white candy gloss (sheen, corner glints, dash) on a painted arcade part (0–1). arcade_ribbon 12.0 The swallow-tailed ends (dp) of an arcade window's gold title ribbon — 0 draws a plain gold key. arcade_bar_ticks 6 How many chunks the arcade looks split a GoBar into when it leaves that to the look (segments = -1) — 0 keeps bars smooth.","",-1],[19,"subclass-the-skin-optional","Subclass the skin (optional)",1,"Only what theme and shape cannot reach — the joystick's hexagon, slot badges, the coach mark's targeting bracket — lives in a skin. Subclass GoSkin, override just those methods, and point the JSON's skin at that resource. A colour-only theme skips this step. A check keeps the promise. tools/check_scaffold.sh creates a throwaway theme every run — changes the accent, sets the radius to 4 — and verifies generation, token propagation and a clean contrast pass before removing it. The first run found a theme with only its accent changed failing 8 pairs: the builder pushed text colours but used the accent as written. It now pushes the accent and the label on it too.","",-1],[20,"same-hue-text-on-a-same-hue-tint","Same-hue text on a same-hue tint",1,"This trap appeared three times in this codebase — pressed buttons (accent panel, accent label), danger buttons, and chips. It looks good in a swatch and collapses the moment it is measured, because the two share a hue and so have no difference in lightness. Label colours are therefore not chosen by hand. The theme builder and GoSkin each push lightness — and only lightness — until the threshold is cleared on the panel the text actually sits on. Hue and saturation survive, so the palette keeps its character and changing it keeps its contrast.","",-1],[20,"colour-read-as-text-and-colour-painted-as-area-w","Colour read as text and colour painted as area want opposite things",1,"On a light theme a warning colour has to darken to stay readable as text (#96500A). When the bar fill inherits that, the experience bar turns brown. Colour alone cannot fix it: yellow is intrinsically bright, so it clears 3:1 over no grey track at all, and darkening the track makes it worse (1.52 → 1.06). So the two are separated. Colour stays vivid — the palette carries fill-only colours such as warning_vivid. The edge carries the contrast — GoSkin draws a 1dp outline on any fill that cannot reach 3:1 against its track, so \"how full is it\" stays legible. Leaving it out is reported. Without a *_vivid, a fill that comes out dark makes the builder print the bar looks drab — add warning_vivid to the palette. A place that used to degrade silently now says so.","MY_LIGHT = dict( warning=hexc(\"9A5407\"), # read as text warning_vivid=hexc(\"F2A007\"), # painted on the bar )",-1],[20,"a-floating-panel-cannot-know-what-is-behind-it","A floating panel cannot know what is behind it",1,"A HUD is drawn over the game — a snowfield, or a cave. If its panel is translucent, whatever is behind it bleeds through and changes the panel's colour, taking the text contrast down with it. At 82% opacity the dark themes' muted text fell to 3.74:1 over a bright backdrop — below the minimum. So translucent panels are measured with pure white and pure black behind them; those are the worst a game scene can offer. The bundled themes' HUD panel is opaque enough to pass (92%) while keeping the glassy look. For the same reason icon colours are not fixed either. The quick slot's glyph was hard-coded white and measured 1.11:1 on a light theme — it now follows the panel it sits on, exactly as the labels do. Two checkers, two reaches. check_contrast.py reads the theme files; colours a skin mixes while running (chips, slots) are measured by the suite's skin contrast section inside Godot.","",-1],[21,"names","Call an icon by its name",0,"Widgets never hold a picture. They ask for a name, and the icon set in use decides what is drawn — swap the set and every icon changes without touching a line of code. GoUi.icons() is the set in use. A name it cannot draw becomes an empty box that keeps its space, with a warning in debug builds, so a missing icon never shifts a row.","GoStyle.icon_button(GoIconSet.SETTINGS, open_settings) # a button slot.icon_name = GoGameIcons.BACKPACK # a quick slot var mark := GoUi.icons().node(&\"cloud_rain\", 24) # a bare Control, any size",-1],[21,"catalog","Find an icon",0,"Every drawing gohud ships. Search by name or by what it shows, narrow it to a set or a group, and pick an icon to copy its name. Search icons GroupAll groups All 1,287 Default 84 Game 187 Library 1,000 Medieval 16 Show more Names and search words stay English in every language — they are what you type in code.","",-1],[21,"sets","Four sets, one lookup",0,"Every set answers the same call. The big ones are added on top of the set in use. Set Names Constants Turn it on Default 84 GoIconSet Always on Medieval 16 engraved — GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MEDIEVAL_DARK) Game 187 GoGameIcons GoUi.add_icons(GoGameIcons.icon_set()) Library 1,000 GoIconLibrary GoUi.add_icons(GoIconLibrary.icon_set()) The library falls back to the game set and the game set to the default set, so one line makes 1,271 names drawable. A set lists its drawings as paths and reads a file only the first time its name is drawn: adding the library reads a table of paths (about 30 ms on a desktop), not 1,000 textures. Paths are strings, not dependencies. An export that picks resources must include addons/gohud/icons/; the default “export all resources” needs nothing.","GoUi.add_icons(GoIconLibrary.icon_set()) # the library — and the game set under it GoUi.add_icons(GoGameIcons.icon_set()) # or the game set alone",-1],[21,"resolution","How a name is found",0,"One order for every set, so you can tell which drawing wins. Every set's own drawings first — the set in use, then each extra set, then their fallbacks, level by level. A set's own drawing is a texture, a path or an icon-font glyph. If nothing drew it, an alias is tried: gear leads to settings, x to close. One hop only. Still nothing: an empty box that keeps its space. That order is why the medieval preset's engraved sword stays on top when you add the library — its own drawing is found before anyone's fallback.","GoUi.use_preset(GoThemePresets.MEDIEVAL_DARK) GoUi.add_icons(GoIconLibrary.icon_set()) GoUi.icons().texture(&\"sword\") # the medieval engraving — its own drawing comes first GoUi.icons().texture(&\"rocket\") # from the game set GoUi.icons().canonical(&\"gear\") # &\"settings\" — an alias",-1],[21,"swap","Presets, your set and extra sets",0,"Three places decide what is drawn. Call What it does GoUi.use_preset(…) Theme, skin and icon set in one go. Clears config.icons, keeps config.extra_icons. GoUi.config.icons = my_set Replaces the preset's icon set with yours. GoUi.add_icons(set) Adds a set that is looked in after the one in use. It survives preset changes.","",-1],[21,"custom","Your own drawings",0,"Override a few names, add a whole folder, or plug in an icon font — the calling code stays the same. Draw on a 24×24 grid with a white stroke. Color comes from modulate, which can only darken — a black drawing stays black on every theme. Import SVGs as DPITexture so they stay sharp in a 64 dp inventory slot. Icons never mirror in right-to-left languages. Only back and forward change direction, and you choose those by name. An icon font works too: fill font and codepoints. Nothing else changes.","# Override a few names — everything else still comes from the set in use var mine := GoIconSet.new() mine.fallback = GoUi.icons() mine.textures = {GoIconSet.CLOSE: preload(\"res://art/close.svg\")} GoUi.config.icons = mine # A folder of drawings — file name = icon name, each read when first drawn GoUi.config.icons = GoIconSet.from_folder(\"res://art/icons\", GoUi.icons())",-1],[21,"naming","Names, groups and search",0,"The rules the bundled sets follow, and the calls that find a name. lower_snake_case, the thing drawn first and its state last: volume_off, battery_charging, arrow_bar_left. No group prefixes. Groups are data, so a name stays the same wherever it is filed. Library names are Tabler's names with underscores: cloud-rain on tabler.io is cloud_rain here. Tabler's names for drawings gohud already had lead there as aliases (shopping_cart → cart). A synonym is an alias, never a second drawing.","",-1],[21,"search","search()",1,"","var icons := GoUi.icons() icons.search(\"arrow left\", 5) # best matches first: back, arrow_bar_left … icons.search(\"rain\") # cloud_rain, then drawings tagged \"rain\"",184],[21,"group-names-names-in-group","group_names() · names_in_group()",1,"","icons.group_names() # every group key, in lookup order icons.names_in_group(&\"weather\") # one group, in display order — every set's share of it icons.group_title(&\"weather\") # \"Weather & sky\"",184],[21,"canonical-has-icon","canonical() · has_icon()",1,"","icons.canonical(&\"gear\") # &\"settings\" icons.canonical(&\"treasure_chest\") # &\"chest\" — Tabler's name for a game drawing icons.has_icon(&\"cloud_rain\") # true once the library is added — nothing is loaded to answer",184],[21,"license","Where the drawings come from",0,"Everything is MIT. The notices travel in the ZIP as THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. Set Source License Default Drawn for gohud MIT Medieval Drawn for gohud MIT Game 171 from Tabler Icons 3.46.0, 16 drawn for gohud MIT Library Tabler Icons 3.46.0 MIT If you plug in someone else's icons, write their source in GoIconSet.attribution — and keep commercial icon fonts inside your game, not in a fork you publish.","",-1]]};
